{"type":"message","id":"163f0a0c","parentId":"d403b965","timestamp":"2026-03-29T12:54:39.827Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to clear historical sessions. I can see there are 78 total subagent sessions, and all of them are \"done\" or \"failed\" (no active ones). \n\nThe subagents tool can kill subagents. But it seems to only kill active ones. The \"recent\" list shows all as done.\n\nLooking at the tool description for `subagents`:\n- action: \"list\" | \"kill\" | \"steer\"\n- recentMinutes: filter by recent activity\n\nThe user wants to clear/clean up the historical sessions. I should try to kill the done ones. Let me try killing some of them to see if it works.\n\nActually, I don't think there's a direct way to delete/bulk delete session history through the API. The subagent sessions are already done - they just remain in the history. Let me think about what \"清理历史session\" means.\n\nMaybe the user wants me to:\n1. Clear/reset the current session (but we're in the main session)\n2. Delete the subagent session files from disk\n3. Something else\n\nLooking at the sessions, they have transcript paths like `/home/node/.openclaw/agents/lucus/sessions/f0a57948-c6f9-4884-a906-2c0364727329.jsonl`. I could potentially delete those files.\n\nBut wait - let me re-read the request: \"清理一下历史session吧\" - this sounds like they want to clear/clean up the session history, probably the subagent sessions that are done.\n\nLet me try to kill the done subagents using the subagents tool with kill action. If that doesn't work, I'll explain what options we have.\n\nActually, looking at the subagents tool more carefully - it says \"for this requester session\" so it only works on subagents of the current session. And they're already done. The kill action is probably for killing active subagents.\n\n\nI should attempt to kill the done sessions anyway to see if the tool accepts that, then report back what succeeded or failed.","think