{"type":"message","id":"1e0c9197","parentId":"4101af8e","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:04:36.070Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So there's an openclaw-gateway running. The issue might be that when I run `openclaw feishu` commands via exec, the command tries to connect to the gateway and there's some kind of conflict or deadlock.\n\nLet me check if the feishu tool is available through the gateway, not through exec. Actually, looking at the sessions_list output earlier, the subagent sessions showed they were using feishu_doc tool successfully (they got responses, just the feishu API returned permission errors).\n\nWait, looking back at the subagent history - the subagents DID call the feishu_doc tool. The tool IS available to subagents. The issue was that the feishu app doesn't have the `docx:document:create` permission.\n\n\nThe subagents weren't actually failing - they were completing successfully, but the feishu API returned a permission error when trying to create a document. Rather than spawning another subagent, I should have just explained this permission issue directly to the user.","thinkingSignature":"4497210caa7f17ceebf034ca9fd14f6f1c1441b37af390f65a8d3b2d59fcde0e"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_sqnx4yuz76ku_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"pgrep -a openclaw | head -5","timeout":5}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":51107,"output":249,"cacheRead":11030,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":62386,"cost":{"input":0.0153321,"output":0.0002988,"cacheRead":0.0006617999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0162927}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774789466574,"responseId":"0618565b48fa646af76a317872cc62c7"}}
