{"type":"message","id":"fa37d8f3","parentId":"1c3f22c9","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:09:53.740Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"python-docx is not installed. Let me try using zipfile to extract the content since docx is a zip file.","thinkingSignature":"6a923c62b107163e038db0036a9626dae288e747cc6902b86ea07b804facb333"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_cafjy58e7c2k_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport zipfile\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\n\npath = '/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/ECHOå_çº_æ_å---b2466f79-4d40-43e5-9081-651cbfbc8dea.docx'\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(path, 'r') as z:\n    with z.open('word/document.xml') as f:\n        tree = ET.parse(f)\n        root = tree.getroot()\n        # Extract all text\n        ns = 'http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main'\n        texts = []\n        for elem in root.iter(f'{{{ns}}}t'):\n            if elem.text:\n                texts.append(elem.text)\n        # Also get paragraphs\n        for para in root.iter(f'{{{ns}}}p'):\n            para_text = ''\n            for t in para.iter(f'{{{ns}}}t'):\n                if t.text:\n                    para_text += t.text\n            if para_text.strip():\n                texts.append(para_text)\n        \n        result = '\\n'.join(texts)\n        print(result[:20000])\nEOF","timeout":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":53871,"output":302,"cacheRead":11562,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":65735,"cost":{"input":0.0161613,"output":0.00036239999999999997,"cacheRead":0.00069372,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.017217419999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774789786706,"responseId":"0618579b6438d19e99a007d212f26780"}}
{"type":"message","id":"726499bf","parentId":"fa37d8f3","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:09:53.891Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_cafjy58e7c2k_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ECHO合约接口\n1. \nECHO 接口\n1.1 \n资产创建和租用\nSolidity\n// 创建一个原创token\n/// @dev Mint an original ECHO token.\nfunction\n mint(string \nmemory\n _uri) external; \n // 创建一个衍生品\n \n/// @dev Mint a derivative ECHO token.\nfunction\n createDerivative(string \nmemory\n _uri, EchoAsset[] \nmemory\n parents) external \npayable\n;\n// 租赁使用权接口（购买使用次数/时长）\n/// @dev Starts renting a token for '_useTimes' units of rental duration.\nfunction\n rentEcho(uint256 tokenId, uint256 _useTimes) external \npayable\n;\n \n // 主动授权一个用户为使用者（赠送使用次数）\n/// @dev Authorizes an account as a user.\n    \nfunction\n authorizedAsUser(address _user, uint256 tokenId, uint256 _useTimes) external;\n// 自衍生接口：用自己的资产衍生一个新资产，省略自付费和自授权过程\n/**\n * @notice Self-derives a child token from multiple newly minted parent tokens.\n * @dev This function allows the caller to mint multiple parent tokens and a child token in a single transaction,\n *      and establishes derivation relationships between the child and each parent token.\n * \n * Requirements:\n * - `parentsUris` must contain at least one URI for the parent tokens.\n * - `childUri` is the URI for the child token.\n * \n * @param parentsUris An array of strings representing the URIs for each parent token to be minted.\n * @param childUri A string representing the URI for the child token to be minted.\n * \n * Example:\n * - If `parentsUris` contains URIs [\"parent1.json\", \"parent2.json\"] and `childUri` is \"child.json\",\n *   this function will mint two parent tokens with the specified URIs and one child token with its URI,\n *   then establish derivation relationships between the child token and each parent token.\n */\nfunction\n selfDerive(string[] \nmemory\n parentsUris, string \nmemory\n childUri) \npublic\n {\n    uint256 len \n=\n parentsUris.length;\n    uint256[] \nmemory\n parentsTokenIds \n=\n \nnew\n uint256[](len);\n    \n// 1. Mint parents token \n    for (uint256 i \n=\n \n0\n; i \n<\n len; i\n++\n) {\n        uint256 _tokenId \n=\n \n++\n_nextTokenId; \n        _mint(_msgSender(), _tokenId, parentsUris[i], true);\n        parentsTokenIds[i] \n=\n _tokenId;\n    }\n    \n// 2. Mint child token\n    uint256 _childTokenId \n=\n \n++\n_nextTokenId;\n    _mint(_msgSender(), _childTokenId, childUri, true);\n    \n// 3. Build derivation relationship\n    for (uint256 i \n=\n \n0\n; i \n<\n len; i\n++\n) {\n        addParent(\n            _childTokenId, \n            EchoAsset({\n                tokenId\n:\n parentsTokenIds[i],\n                assetContract\n:\n address(\nthis\n)\n            })\n        );\n        addChild(\n            parentsTokenIds[i], \n            EchoAsset({\n                tokenId\n:\n _childTokenId,\n                assetContract\n:\n address(\nthis\n)\n            })\n        );\n    }\n}\n// 注意⚠️ 只有拓展场景的合约没有衍生品创建接口，只有 mint 接口\n1.2 \n费用、状态设置更新\nTypeScript\n// 方法：设置单位租赁周期的费用和租赁类型\n/**\n * @dev Sets the cost of one unit rental period and the rentalType for a 'tokenId'.\n * \n * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n * @param _feesInWei The cost of one unit rental period, which is in wei.\n * @param _durationInSeconds The duration of one unit rental period, which is in seconds.\n * @param _paymentToken The payment method. If pay with ETH, use address(0).\n * \n * Emits a {RentalInfoSet} event.\n */\nfunction\n updateRentalInfo(uint256 tokenId, uint256 _feesInWei, uint256 _durationInSeconds, address _paymentToken) \nexternal\n;\n//  方法：拓展权限开关设置、以及允许最大分润比例设置\n    /**\n     * @dev Sets whether the ECHO token 'tokenId' can be extended and the maximum share allowed for extension.\n     * \n     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token.\n     * @param extensible A boolean indicating whether the token can be extended.\n     * @param allowedShare The maximum share allowed for extension.\n     * \n     */\n    \nfunction\n setExtensible(uint256 tokenId, bool extensible, uint256 allowedShare) \nexternal\n;\n// 衍生条款：记录衍生收费信息\n    \nstruct\n DerivativeTerms {\n        uint256 upfrontFee;     \n// One-time derivation fee, upfront cost (in wei) to create a derivative of this token.\n        address paymentToken; \n// The token address to pay the upfront fee.\n        uint256 usageRoyalty;   \n// Share of revenue (in basis points, 100 = 1%) from the usage of this token's derivatives.\n    }\n    \n// 方法： 更新衍生条款   \n    \n/**\n     * @notice Sets the derivative terms and enables/disables derivation for a specific token.\n     * @notice Only update terms if derivation is enabled.\n     * @notice If disabling, pass in empty ‘terms’ (all zeroes).\n     * @dev Only the owner or an approved operator of the token can call this function.\n     * \n     * @param tokenId The token ID for which to set derivative terms.\n     * @param enabled Boolean indicating whether to enable (true) or disable (false) derivation.\n     * @param terms The DerivativeTerms struct containing upfront fee, payment token, and usage royalty.           \n     * \n     * Emits either a {DerivationEnabled} or {DerivationDisabled} event based on the 'enabled' parameter.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n setDerivTerms(uint256 tokenId, bool enabled, DerivativeTerms \ncalldata\n terms) \nexternal\n;   \n// 使用内容更新\n/// @dev Sets the protected source URI of a token.\nfunction\n setProtectedSourceURI(uint256 tokenId, string \nmemory\n puri) \npublic\n {\n    _setProtectedSourceURI(tokenId, puri);\n}\n// 蓝图更新\n/// @dev Sets the blueprint URI of a token.\nfunction\n setBlueprintURI(uint256 tokenId, string \nmemory\n buri) \npublic\n {\n    _setBlueprintURI(tokenId, buri);\n}\n1.3 \n使用权管理\nSolidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma\n solidity ^0.8.20;\nimport\n {\nIERC165\n} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/introspection/IERC165.sol\";\nimport\n {\nIERC721\n} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol\";\ninterface\n IECHO \nis\n \nIERC165\n, \nIERC721\n {\n    \n// Structs\n// 使用权租赁类型：默认类型Unknown，基于次数，基于时长\n    \n/**\n     * @dev The rental type will be determined based on the value of the rental duration.\n     * If 'duration' = 0, rentalType = TimesBased; If 'duration' != 0, rentalType = DurationBased. \n     */\n    enum \nRentalType\n { Unknown, TimesBased, DurationBased }\n    \n// 租赁信息类型：租赁费用、租赁类型、支付方式等\n     \n/**\n     * @dev A type that records the rental info for each tokenId. \n     *  If duration = 0，indicates that the charges are times-based rental.\n     *  If duration != 0，indicates that the charges are duration-based rental.\n     *\n     * @param unitFee The cost of one unit rental period, which is in wei.\n     * @param duration The duration of one unit rental period, which is in seconds.\n     * @param rentalType The rental type will be determined based on the value of the rental duration.\n     *   If 'duration' = 0, rentalType = TimesBased; If 'duration' != 0, rentalType = DurationBased.\n     * @param paymentToken If pay with ETH, use address(0) as paymentToken.\n     */\n    \nstruct\n RentalInfo {\n        uint256 unitFee;\n        uint32 duration;\n        RentalType rentalType;\n        address paymentToken;\n    }\n// 使用状态类型：\n基于时长使用类型类型的使用状态\n    \n/**\n     * @dev A type that records the usage status for each tokenId.\n     * \n@notice Only used in DurationBased rental type.\n     * \n     * @param currentUser The current user of the NFT.\n     * @param leaseStartTime The start time for a rental.\n     * @param leaseEndTime The end time for a rental.\n     * @param durationUnits Number of duration units purchased for the lease period.\n     * @param lastUsedAt The last time the ECHO was used by the current user.\n     */\n    \nstruct\n UseStatus {\n        address currentUser;\n        uint256 leaseStartTime;\n        uint256 leaseEndTime;\n        uint256 durationUnits;\n        uint256 lastUsedAt;\n    }\n    \n// errors\n// 自定义错误：零使用次数，次数为0时出发（TimesBased）\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Indicates the use times of a user for tokenId is zero. In case of TimesBased rental type.\n     */\n    \nerror\n ZeroUseTimes(address user, uint256 tokenId);\n// 自定义错误：使用次数不足（TimesBased）\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Indicates the user has insufficient use times for the 'tokenId'.\n     */\n    \nerror\n InsufficientUseTimes(address user, uint256 tokenId, uint256 neededTimes, uint256 remainingTimes);\n// 自定义错误：使用者非法或租赁到期（TimesBased）\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Indicates a user is not the valid user of tokenId, or the rental has expired.\n     */\n    \nerror\n InvalidUserOrExpired(address validUser, uint256 expiryTime, address checkedUser, uint256 checkedAt);\n    \n// 自定义错误：0地址错误\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when the address provided is the zero address.\n     */\n    \nerror\n CanNotBeZeroAddress();\n// 自定义错误：所有者未开启使用权租赁\n，Rental type is Unknown\n    \n/**  \n     * @dev Rental type is Unknown. The owner has not opened for use yet.\n     */\n    \nerror\n RentalInactive();\n    \n// 自定义错误：如果有合法使用者（还有次数/还有时长）存在，RentalType 禁止更改\n    \n/**\n     * @dev If valid users exists, rental type update is forbidden.\n     */\n    \nerror\n RentalTypeUpdateForbidden();\n// 自定义错误：状态检查，当前有合法租赁者\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Indicates the lease period of current user has not expired for the current `tokenId`. \n     * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n     * @param currentUser The current user of the 'tokenId'.\n     */\n    \nerror\n UnderLease(uint256 tokenId, address currentUser);\n  // 自定义错误：状态检查，租赁状态未开启\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Indicates that the rentable status of a token is false.\n     * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n     * @param isRentable Rentable status of a token.\n     */\n    \nerror\n RentalClosed(uint256 tokenId, bool isRentable);\n    \n// Events\n // 事件：owner授权一个使用者时出触发\n     \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the owner authorized a 'user' account as the user of 'tokenId'.\n     * @param user The account authorized to use the ECHO.\n     * @param tokenId The token which the 'user' is authorized to.\n     * @param rentalType The rental type of the 'tokenId'.\n     * @param useTimes Indicates the number of units for the rental duration, or the use times in case of times-based. \n     * @notice This will allow the 'user' to use the ECHO for free.\n     */\n    \nevent\n UserAuthorized(address \nindexed\n user, uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, RentalType \nindexed\n rentalType, uint256 useTimes);\n// 事件：暂停租赁，当租赁暂停时触发\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the owner of 'tokenId' pause the rental.\n     * @param tokenId The token will to be paused.\n     * @param opertator It will be the owner of token.\n     * \n     * \nNOTE\n: This function will not affect the usage rights that have already been obtained.\n     * It will only affect whether new rentals can be initiated. \n     * If a Duration-based rental exists and the lease period has not expired, rental can not be paused.\n     */\n    \nevent\n RentalPaused(uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, address opertator);\n// 事件：租金信息设置时触发\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the rental info for a 'tokenId' is set.\n     * \n     */\n    \nevent\n RentalInfoSet(uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, uint256 unitFee, uint256 duration, RentalType rentalType, address paymentToken);\n// 事件：ECHO被使用时触发    \n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the 'user' uses a ECHO.\n     * @param echoConsumer TThe address of the consumer contract that will use the ECHO token.\n     * @param user The actual account using the usage rights of the token.\n     * @param tokenId The token which the 'user' use.\n     * @param amount The amount of ECHO used.\n     */\n    \nevent\n ECHOUsed(address \nindexed\n echoConsumer, address \nindexed\n user, uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, uint256 amount);\n// 事件：受保护资源索引更新时触发\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the protected source of 'tokenId' is updated.\n     * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n     */\n    \nevent\n ProtectedSourceUpdated(uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId);\n// 事件：蓝图更新\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the blueprint of 'tokenId' is updated.\n     * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n     */\n    \nevent\n BlueprintUpdated(uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId);\n    \n    \n// Functions\n// 方法：设置单位租赁周期的费用和租赁类型\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Sets the cost of one unit rental period and the rentalType for a 'tokenId'.\n     * \n     * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n     * @param _feesInWei The cost of one unit rental period, which is in wei.\n     * @param _durationInSeconds The duration of one unit rental period, which is in seconds.\n     * @param _paymentToken The payment method. If pay with ETH, use address(0).\n     * \n     * Emits a {RentalInfoSet} event.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n updateRentalInfo(uint256 tokenId, uint256 _feesInWei, uint256 _durationInSeconds, address _paymentToken) \nexternal\n;\n// 方法：暂停租赁，所有者暂停租赁，该方法不影响当前使用者权益，当拥有基于时长使用者时不可暂停\n    \n/** \n     * @dev The owner of 'tokenId' can pause the rental, but it will not affect the usage rights\n     * that have already been obtained. It will only affect whether new rentals can be initiated.\n     * \n     * If a Duration-based rental exists and the lease period has not expired, rental can not be paused.\n     * \n     * Emits a {RentalPaused} event.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n pauseRental(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n;\n// 方法：获取当前tokenId的使用者列表\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Get the current users of the 'tokenId'.\n     * @dev In case of times-based, this returns all user whose 'useTimes'\n     * @dev TimesBased rental: Returns a dynamically sized address array representing all users.\n     * @dev DurationBased and the default case: return an array with a fixed length of 1.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n userOf(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (address[] \nmemory\n);\n// 方法：场景内使用ECHO\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Use the 'tokenId' ECHO.\n     * \n     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.\n     * \n     */\n    \nfunction\n useECHO(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n returns (string \nmemory\n);\n// 方法：查看当前token是否开启租赁\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Get the rentable status of the specified 'tokenID'. \n     * \n     * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n getRentableStatus(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (bool);\n// 方法：查看当前token的租金设置情况\n     \n/**\n     * @dev Get the rental info of a token, including (unitFee, duration, rentalType, paymentToken).\n     */\n    \nfunction\n getRentalInfo(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (RentalInfo \nmemory\n);\n    \n// 方法：获取某 user 在某 tokenId 上的剩余使用次数\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Get the remaining use times of a 'user_' for the 'tokenId_'.\n     * @dev Only used in TimesBased rental type.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n getRemainingTimes(address user_, uint256 tokenId_) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (uint256 remainingTimes);\n// 方法：获取某tokenId的总剩余使用次数\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Get the total use times of the 'tokenId_'.\n     * @dev Only used in TimesBased rental type.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n getTotalLeftTimes(uint256 tokenId_) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (uint256);\n// 方法：获取某tokenId的使用状态（DurationBased）\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Get the current user and the expiration time of the 'tokenId_'.\n     * @dev Only used in DurationBased rental type.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n getUseStatus(uint256 tokenId_) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (UseStatus \nmemory\n);\n    \n // 方法：检查当前租赁类型是否可更改  \n    \n/**\n     * @dev Determine if the rental type of 'tokenId' can be \nchanged\n.\n     *  If a valid user exsit, rental type can not be \nchanged\n. \n     */\n    \nfunction\n canChangeRentalType(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (bool);\n// 方法：获取受保护资源索引\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Get the protected source URI of the 'tokenId'.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n protectedSourceURI(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (string \nmemory\n);\n// 方法：获取蓝图    \n    \n/**\n     * @dev Returns the Blueprint Uniform Resource Identifier (BURI) for `tokenId` token.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n blueprintURI(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (string \nmemory\n);\n}\n1.4 \n 可租赁+分润模块\nSolidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n// DimAI ECHO Contracts (last updated v1.0.0) (/ECHO/extensions/interfaces/IECHORentable.sol)\npragma\n solidity ^0.8.20;\nimport\n {\nIECHO\n} from \"../../IECHO.sol\";\ninterface\n IECHORentable \nis\n \nIECHO\n {\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when attempting to settle pending rental for a DurationBased token before the rental has ended.\n     */\n    \nerror\n RentalNotEnded();\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when the rental type is DurationBased but the function is called with a times-based token.\n     */\n    \nerror\n DurationBasedOnly();\n// 事件：购买使用权（租赁某个token）时触发\n      \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when a 'user' starts renting an ECHO 'tokenId'.\n     * @param user The account who want to lease the ECHO.\n     * @param tokenId The token which the 'user' want to lease.\n     * @param rentalType The rental type of the 'tokenId'.\n     * @param useTimes Indicates the number of units for the rental duration, or the use times in case of times-based. \n     */\n    \nevent\n EchoRented(address \nindexed\n user, uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, RentalType \nindexed\n rentalType, uint256 useTimes);\n// 事件：使用时触发分润（给使用资产的owner的分润）\n      \n/**\n     * @notice Non-derivation scenarios only.\n     * @dev Emitted when usage revenue is distributed to the owner only.\n     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token for which the usage revenue was distributed.\n     * @param paymentToken The address of the payment token used for the revenue.\n     * @param ownerShare The amount of rental fee distributed to the owner.\n     */\n    \nevent\n RevenueDistributedBase(\n        uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, \n        address \nindexed\n paymentToken, \n        uint256 ownerShare\n    );\n    \n// 方法：清算基于时长的租赁可能剩余的未释放的租金分润\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Settles any remaining pending rental after the rental period ends,\n     *     only for DurationBased rentals.\n     * \n     * Requirements:\n     * - The caller must be the owner of the tokenId.\n     * - The rental type must be `DurationBased`.\n     * - The current time must be after the rental end time.\n     * - There must be a non-zero pending rental balance.\n     * - Must be overridden in derivation sceneio.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n settleRemainingRental(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n;\n}\n1.5 \n 拓展权授权（主动授权逻辑）\nSolidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n// DimAI ECHO Contracts (last updated v1.0.0) (/ECHO/extensions/interfaces/IECHOPermissioned.sol)\npragma\n solidity ^0.8.20;\nimport\n {\nIECHO\n} from \"../../IECHO.sol\";\ninterface\n IECHOPermissioned \nis\n \nIECHO\n {\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Enum representing the way to obtain the permission in a consumption scenario,\n     *   whether it is OwnerDirect or RequestBased.\n     * \n     * - None: no permission obtained\n     * - OwnerDirect: Owner approved directly\n     * - RequestBased: obtain permission by request\n     */\n    enum \nPermissionType\n { None, OwnerDirect, RequestBased }\n    \n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when attempting to enable an extension on a non-extensible token.\n     */\n    \nerror\n NotExtensible(uint256 tokenId);\n    \n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when the caller is not the expected address.\n     */\n    \nerror\n CallerMismatch(address operator, address expected);\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when a consumer contract attempts to use an ECHO token without permission.\n     */\n \n    \nerror\n NotPermissioned(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId);\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when a duplicate consumer contract is approved.\n     */\n    \nerror\n ConsumerAlreadyApproved(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer);\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when attempting to operate on a permission (e.g., revoke) \n     * for `echoConsumer` on `tokenId`, but the actual PermissionType does not match the required one.\n     */\n    \nerror\n PermissionTypeError( uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer, PermissionType needed, PermissionType actual);\n// 事件：拓展属性更新\n     \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the extensibility of a given 'tokenId' is set or \nchanged\n.\n     */\n    \nevent\n ExtensibilityUpdated(address \nindexed\n operator, uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, bool extensible, uint256 allowedShare);\n// 事件：许可授权    \n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when usage permission for a given ‘tokenId’ is approved to an ‘echoConsumer’ contract.\n     */\n    \nevent\n PermissionApproved(address \nindexed\n operator, address \nindexed\n echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId);\n// 事件：许可撤销\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the permission of an 'echoConsumer' is revoked for a specific 'tokenId'.\n     */\n    \nevent\n PermissionRevoked(address \nindexed\n operator, address \nindexed\n echoConsumer, uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId);\n// 方法：拓展场景使用echo的接口\n    \n/**\n     * @d"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":145,"aggregated":"ECHO合约接口\n1. \nECHO 接口\n1.1 \n资产创建和租用\nSolidity\n// 创建一个原创token\n/// @dev Mint an original ECHO token.\nfunction\n mint(string \nmemory\n _uri) external; \n // 创建一个衍生品\n \n/// @dev Mint a derivative ECHO token.\nfunction\n createDerivative(string \nmemory\n _uri, EchoAsset[] \nmemory\n parents) external \npayable\n;\n// 租赁使用权接口（购买使用次数/时长）\n/// @dev Starts renting a token for '_useTimes' units of rental duration.\nfunction\n rentEcho(uint256 tokenId, uint256 _useTimes) external \npayable\n;\n \n // 主动授权一个用户为使用者（赠送使用次数）\n/// @dev Authorizes an account as a user.\n    \nfunction\n authorizedAsUser(address _user, uint256 tokenId, uint256 _useTimes) external;\n// 自衍生接口：用自己的资产衍生一个新资产，省略自付费和自授权过程\n/**\n * @notice Self-derives a child token from multiple newly minted parent tokens.\n * @dev This function allows the caller to mint multiple parent tokens and a child token in a single transaction,\n *      and establishes derivation relationships between the child and each parent token.\n * \n * Requirements:\n * - `parentsUris` must contain at least one URI for the parent tokens.\n * - `childUri` is the URI for the child token.\n * \n * @param parentsUris An array of strings representing the URIs for each parent token to be minted.\n * @param childUri A string representing the URI for the child token to be minted.\n * \n * Example:\n * - If `parentsUris` contains URIs [\"parent1.json\", \"parent2.json\"] and `childUri` is \"child.json\",\n *   this function will mint two parent tokens with the specified URIs and one child token with its URI,\n *   then establish derivation relationships between the child token and each parent token.\n */\nfunction\n selfDerive(string[] \nmemory\n parentsUris, string \nmemory\n childUri) \npublic\n {\n    uint256 len \n=\n parentsUris.length;\n    uint256[] \nmemory\n parentsTokenIds \n=\n \nnew\n uint256[](len);\n    \n// 1. Mint parents token \n    for (uint256 i \n=\n \n0\n; i \n<\n len; i\n++\n) {\n        uint256 _tokenId \n=\n \n++\n_nextTokenId; \n        _mint(_msgSender(), _tokenId, parentsUris[i], true);\n        parentsTokenIds[i] \n=\n _tokenId;\n    }\n    \n// 2. Mint child token\n    uint256 _childTokenId \n=\n \n++\n_nextTokenId;\n    _mint(_msgSender(), _childTokenId, childUri, true);\n    \n// 3. Build derivation relationship\n    for (uint256 i \n=\n \n0\n; i \n<\n len; i\n++\n) {\n        addParent(\n            _childTokenId, \n            EchoAsset({\n                tokenId\n:\n parentsTokenIds[i],\n                assetContract\n:\n address(\nthis\n)\n            })\n        );\n        addChild(\n            parentsTokenIds[i], \n            EchoAsset({\n                tokenId\n:\n _childTokenId,\n                assetContract\n:\n address(\nthis\n)\n            })\n        );\n    }\n}\n// 注意⚠️ 只有拓展场景的合约没有衍生品创建接口，只有 mint 接口\n1.2 \n费用、状态设置更新\nTypeScript\n// 方法：设置单位租赁周期的费用和租赁类型\n/**\n * @dev Sets the cost of one unit rental period and the rentalType for a 'tokenId'.\n * \n * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n * @param _feesInWei The cost of one unit rental period, which is in wei.\n * @param _durationInSeconds The duration of one unit rental period, which is in seconds.\n * @param _paymentToken The payment method. If pay with ETH, use address(0).\n * \n * Emits a {RentalInfoSet} event.\n */\nfunction\n updateRentalInfo(uint256 tokenId, uint256 _feesInWei, uint256 _durationInSeconds, address _paymentToken) \nexternal\n;\n//  方法：拓展权限开关设置、以及允许最大分润比例设置\n    /**\n     * @dev Sets whether the ECHO token 'tokenId' can be extended and the maximum share allowed for extension.\n     * \n     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token.\n     * @param extensible A boolean indicating whether the token can be extended.\n     * @param allowedShare The maximum share allowed for extension.\n     * \n     */\n    \nfunction\n setExtensible(uint256 tokenId, bool extensible, uint256 allowedShare) \nexternal\n;\n// 衍生条款：记录衍生收费信息\n    \nstruct\n DerivativeTerms {\n        uint256 upfrontFee;     \n// One-time derivation fee, upfront cost (in wei) to create a derivative of this token.\n        address paymentToken; \n// The token address to pay the upfront fee.\n        uint256 usageRoyalty;   \n// Share of revenue (in basis points, 100 = 1%) from the usage of this token's derivatives.\n    }\n    \n// 方法： 更新衍生条款   \n    \n/**\n     * @notice Sets the derivative terms and enables/disables derivation for a specific token.\n     * @notice Only update terms if derivation is enabled.\n     * @notice If disabling, pass in empty ‘terms’ (all zeroes).\n     * @dev Only the owner or an approved operator of the token can call this function.\n     * \n     * @param tokenId The token ID for which to set derivative terms.\n     * @param enabled Boolean indicating whether to enable (true) or disable (false) derivation.\n     * @param terms The DerivativeTerms struct containing upfront fee, payment token, and usage royalty.           \n     * \n     * Emits either a {DerivationEnabled} or {DerivationDisabled} event based on the 'enabled' parameter.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n setDerivTerms(uint256 tokenId, bool enabled, DerivativeTerms \ncalldata\n terms) \nexternal\n;   \n// 使用内容更新\n/// @dev Sets the protected source URI of a token.\nfunction\n setProtectedSourceURI(uint256 tokenId, string \nmemory\n puri) \npublic\n {\n    _setProtectedSourceURI(tokenId, puri);\n}\n// 蓝图更新\n/// @dev Sets the blueprint URI of a token.\nfunction\n setBlueprintURI(uint256 tokenId, string \nmemory\n buri) \npublic\n {\n    _setBlueprintURI(tokenId, buri);\n}\n1.3 \n使用权管理\nSolidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma\n solidity ^0.8.20;\nimport\n {\nIERC165\n} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/introspection/IERC165.sol\";\nimport\n {\nIERC721\n} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol\";\ninterface\n IECHO \nis\n \nIERC165\n, \nIERC721\n {\n    \n// Structs\n// 使用权租赁类型：默认类型Unknown，基于次数，基于时长\n    \n/**\n     * @dev The rental type will be determined based on the value of the rental duration.\n     * If 'duration' = 0, rentalType = TimesBased; If 'duration' != 0, rentalType = DurationBased. \n     */\n    enum \nRentalType\n { Unknown, TimesBased, DurationBased }\n    \n// 租赁信息类型：租赁费用、租赁类型、支付方式等\n     \n/**\n     * @dev A type that records the rental info for each tokenId. \n     *  If duration = 0，indicates that the charges are times-based rental.\n     *  If duration != 0，indicates that the charges are duration-based rental.\n     *\n     * @param unitFee The cost of one unit rental period, which is in wei.\n     * @param duration The duration of one unit rental period, which is in seconds.\n     * @param rentalType The rental type will be determined based on the value of the rental duration.\n     *   If 'duration' = 0, rentalType = TimesBased; If 'duration' != 0, rentalType = DurationBased.\n     * @param paymentToken If pay with ETH, use address(0) as paymentToken.\n     */\n    \nstruct\n RentalInfo {\n        uint256 unitFee;\n        uint32 duration;\n        RentalType rentalType;\n        address paymentToken;\n    }\n// 使用状态类型：\n基于时长使用类型类型的使用状态\n    \n/**\n     * @dev A type that records the usage status for each tokenId.\n     * \n@notice Only used in DurationBased rental type.\n     * \n     * @param currentUser The current user of the NFT.\n     * @param leaseStartTime The start time for a rental.\n     * @param leaseEndTime The end time for a rental.\n     * @param durationUnits Number of duration units purchased for the lease period.\n     * @param lastUsedAt The last time the ECHO was used by the current user.\n     */\n    \nstruct\n UseStatus {\n        address currentUser;\n        uint256 leaseStartTime;\n        uint256 leaseEndTime;\n        uint256 durationUnits;\n        uint256 lastUsedAt;\n    }\n    \n// errors\n// 自定义错误：零使用次数，次数为0时出发（TimesBased）\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Indicates the use times of a user for tokenId is zero. In case of TimesBased rental type.\n     */\n    \nerror\n ZeroUseTimes(address user, uint256 tokenId);\n// 自定义错误：使用次数不足（TimesBased）\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Indicates the user has insufficient use times for the 'tokenId'.\n     */\n    \nerror\n InsufficientUseTimes(address user, uint256 tokenId, uint256 neededTimes, uint256 remainingTimes);\n// 自定义错误：使用者非法或租赁到期（TimesBased）\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Indicates a user is not the valid user of tokenId, or the rental has expired.\n     */\n    \nerror\n InvalidUserOrExpired(address validUser, uint256 expiryTime, address checkedUser, uint256 checkedAt);\n    \n// 自定义错误：0地址错误\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when the address provided is the zero address.\n     */\n    \nerror\n CanNotBeZeroAddress();\n// 自定义错误：所有者未开启使用权租赁\n，Rental type is Unknown\n    \n/**  \n     * @dev Rental type is Unknown. The owner has not opened for use yet.\n     */\n    \nerror\n RentalInactive();\n    \n// 自定义错误：如果有合法使用者（还有次数/还有时长）存在，RentalType 禁止更改\n    \n/**\n     * @dev If valid users exists, rental type update is forbidden.\n     */\n    \nerror\n RentalTypeUpdateForbidden();\n// 自定义错误：状态检查，当前有合法租赁者\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Indicates the lease period of current user has not expired for the current `tokenId`. \n     * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n     * @param currentUser The current user of the 'tokenId'.\n     */\n    \nerror\n UnderLease(uint256 tokenId, address currentUser);\n  // 自定义错误：状态检查，租赁状态未开启\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Indicates that the rentable status of a token is false.\n     * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n     * @param isRentable Rentable status of a token.\n     */\n    \nerror\n RentalClosed(uint256 tokenId, bool isRentable);\n    \n// Events\n // 事件：owner授权一个使用者时出触发\n     \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the owner authorized a 'user' account as the user of 'tokenId'.\n     * @param user The account authorized to use the ECHO.\n     * @param tokenId The token which the 'user' is authorized to.\n     * @param rentalType The rental type of the 'tokenId'.\n     * @param useTimes Indicates the number of units for the rental duration, or the use times in case of times-based. \n     * @notice This will allow the 'user' to use the ECHO for free.\n     */\n    \nevent\n UserAuthorized(address \nindexed\n user, uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, RentalType \nindexed\n rentalType, uint256 useTimes);\n// 事件：暂停租赁，当租赁暂停时触发\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the owner of 'tokenId' pause the rental.\n     * @param tokenId The token will to be paused.\n     * @param opertator It will be the owner of token.\n     * \n     * \nNOTE\n: This function will not affect the usage rights that have already been obtained.\n     * It will only affect whether new rentals can be initiated. \n     * If a Duration-based rental exists and the lease period has not expired, rental can not be paused.\n     */\n    \nevent\n RentalPaused(uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, address opertator);\n// 事件：租金信息设置时触发\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the rental info for a 'tokenId' is set.\n     * \n     */\n    \nevent\n RentalInfoSet(uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, uint256 unitFee, uint256 duration, RentalType rentalType, address paymentToken);\n// 事件：ECHO被使用时触发    \n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the 'user' uses a ECHO.\n     * @param echoConsumer TThe address of the consumer contract that will use the ECHO token.\n     * @param user The actual account using the usage rights of the token.\n     * @param tokenId The token which the 'user' use.\n     * @param amount The amount of ECHO used.\n     */\n    \nevent\n ECHOUsed(address \nindexed\n echoConsumer, address \nindexed\n user, uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, uint256 amount);\n// 事件：受保护资源索引更新时触发\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the protected source of 'tokenId' is updated.\n     * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n     */\n    \nevent\n ProtectedSourceUpdated(uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId);\n// 事件：蓝图更新\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the blueprint of 'tokenId' is updated.\n     * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n     */\n    \nevent\n BlueprintUpdated(uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId);\n    \n    \n// Functions\n// 方法：设置单位租赁周期的费用和租赁类型\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Sets the cost of one unit rental period and the rentalType for a 'tokenId'.\n     * \n     * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n     * @param _feesInWei The cost of one unit rental period, which is in wei.\n     * @param _durationInSeconds The duration of one unit rental period, which is in seconds.\n     * @param _paymentToken The payment method. If pay with ETH, use address(0).\n     * \n     * Emits a {RentalInfoSet} event.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n updateRentalInfo(uint256 tokenId, uint256 _feesInWei, uint256 _durationInSeconds, address _paymentToken) \nexternal\n;\n// 方法：暂停租赁，所有者暂停租赁，该方法不影响当前使用者权益，当拥有基于时长使用者时不可暂停\n    \n/** \n     * @dev The owner of 'tokenId' can pause the rental, but it will not affect the usage rights\n     * that have already been obtained. It will only affect whether new rentals can be initiated.\n     * \n     * If a Duration-based rental exists and the lease period has not expired, rental can not be paused.\n     * \n     * Emits a {RentalPaused} event.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n pauseRental(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n;\n// 方法：获取当前tokenId的使用者列表\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Get the current users of the 'tokenId'.\n     * @dev In case of times-based, this returns all user whose 'useTimes'\n     * @dev TimesBased rental: Returns a dynamically sized address array representing all users.\n     * @dev DurationBased and the default case: return an array with a fixed length of 1.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n userOf(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (address[] \nmemory\n);\n// 方法：场景内使用ECHO\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Use the 'tokenId' ECHO.\n     * \n     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.\n     * \n     */\n    \nfunction\n useECHO(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n returns (string \nmemory\n);\n// 方法：查看当前token是否开启租赁\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Get the rentable status of the specified 'tokenID'. \n     * \n     * @param tokenId Identifier number of a token.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n getRentableStatus(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (bool);\n// 方法：查看当前token的租金设置情况\n     \n/**\n     * @dev Get the rental info of a token, including (unitFee, duration, rentalType, paymentToken).\n     */\n    \nfunction\n getRentalInfo(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (RentalInfo \nmemory\n);\n    \n// 方法：获取某 user 在某 tokenId 上的剩余使用次数\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Get the remaining use times of a 'user_' for the 'tokenId_'.\n     * @dev Only used in TimesBased rental type.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n getRemainingTimes(address user_, uint256 tokenId_) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (uint256 remainingTimes);\n// 方法：获取某tokenId的总剩余使用次数\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Get the total use times of the 'tokenId_'.\n     * @dev Only used in TimesBased rental type.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n getTotalLeftTimes(uint256 tokenId_) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (uint256);\n// 方法：获取某tokenId的使用状态（DurationBased）\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Get the current user and the expiration time of the 'tokenId_'.\n     * @dev Only used in DurationBased rental type.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n getUseStatus(uint256 tokenId_) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (UseStatus \nmemory\n);\n    \n // 方法：检查当前租赁类型是否可更改  \n    \n/**\n     * @dev Determine if the rental type of 'tokenId' can be \nchanged\n.\n     *  If a valid user exsit, rental type can not be \nchanged\n. \n     */\n    \nfunction\n canChangeRentalType(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (bool);\n// 方法：获取受保护资源索引\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Get the protected source URI of the 'tokenId'.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n protectedSourceURI(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (string \nmemory\n);\n// 方法：获取蓝图    \n    \n/**\n     * @dev Returns the Blueprint Uniform Resource Identifier (BURI) for `tokenId` token.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n blueprintURI(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n \nview\n returns (string \nmemory\n);\n}\n1.4 \n 可租赁+分润模块\nSolidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n// DimAI ECHO Contracts (last updated v1.0.0) (/ECHO/extensions/interfaces/IECHORentable.sol)\npragma\n solidity ^0.8.20;\nimport\n {\nIECHO\n} from \"../../IECHO.sol\";\ninterface\n IECHORentable \nis\n \nIECHO\n {\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when attempting to settle pending rental for a DurationBased token before the rental has ended.\n     */\n    \nerror\n RentalNotEnded();\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when the rental type is DurationBased but the function is called with a times-based token.\n     */\n    \nerror\n DurationBasedOnly();\n// 事件：购买使用权（租赁某个token）时触发\n      \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when a 'user' starts renting an ECHO 'tokenId'.\n     * @param user The account who want to lease the ECHO.\n     * @param tokenId The token which the 'user' want to lease.\n     * @param rentalType The rental type of the 'tokenId'.\n     * @param useTimes Indicates the number of units for the rental duration, or the use times in case of times-based. \n     */\n    \nevent\n EchoRented(address \nindexed\n user, uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, RentalType \nindexed\n rentalType, uint256 useTimes);\n// 事件：使用时触发分润（给使用资产的owner的分润）\n      \n/**\n     * @notice Non-derivation scenarios only.\n     * @dev Emitted when usage revenue is distributed to the owner only.\n     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token for which the usage revenue was distributed.\n     * @param paymentToken The address of the payment token used for the revenue.\n     * @param ownerShare The amount of rental fee distributed to the owner.\n     */\n    \nevent\n RevenueDistributedBase(\n        uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, \n        address \nindexed\n paymentToken, \n        uint256 ownerShare\n    );\n    \n// 方法：清算基于时长的租赁可能剩余的未释放的租金分润\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Settles any remaining pending rental after the rental period ends,\n     *     only for DurationBased rentals.\n     * \n     * Requirements:\n     * - The caller must be the owner of the tokenId.\n     * - The rental type must be `DurationBased`.\n     * - The current time must be after the rental end time.\n     * - There must be a non-zero pending rental balance.\n     * - Must be overridden in derivation sceneio.\n     */\n    \nfunction\n settleRemainingRental(uint256 tokenId) \nexternal\n;\n}\n1.5 \n 拓展权授权（主动授权逻辑）\nSolidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n// DimAI ECHO Contracts (last updated v1.0.0) (/ECHO/extensions/interfaces/IECHOPermissioned.sol)\npragma\n solidity ^0.8.20;\nimport\n {\nIECHO\n} from \"../../IECHO.sol\";\ninterface\n IECHOPermissioned \nis\n \nIECHO\n {\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Enum representing the way to obtain the permission in a consumption scenario,\n     *   whether it is OwnerDirect or RequestBased.\n     * \n     * - None: no permission obtained\n     * - OwnerDirect: Owner approved directly\n     * - RequestBased: obtain permission by request\n     */\n    enum \nPermissionType\n { None, OwnerDirect, RequestBased }\n    \n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when attempting to enable an extension on a non-extensible token.\n     */\n    \nerror\n NotExtensible(uint256 tokenId);\n    \n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when the caller is not the expected address.\n     */\n    \nerror\n CallerMismatch(address operator, address expected);\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when a consumer contract attempts to use an ECHO token without permission.\n     */\n \n    \nerror\n NotPermissioned(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId);\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when a duplicate consumer contract is approved.\n     */\n    \nerror\n ConsumerAlreadyApproved(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer);\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Error thrown when attempting to operate on a permission (e.g., revoke) \n     * for `echoConsumer` on `tokenId`, but the actual PermissionType does not match the required one.\n     */\n    \nerror\n PermissionTypeError( uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer, PermissionType needed, PermissionType actual);\n// 事件：拓展属性更新\n     \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the extensibility of a given 'tokenId' is set or \nchanged\n.\n     */\n    \nevent\n ExtensibilityUpdated(address \nindexed\n operator, uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId, bool extensible, uint256 allowedShare);\n// 事件：许可授权    \n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when usage permission for a given ‘tokenId’ is approved to an ‘echoConsumer’ contract.\n     */\n    \nevent\n PermissionApproved(address \nindexed\n operator, address \nindexed\n echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId);\n// 事件：许可撤销\n    \n/**\n     * @dev Emitted when the permission of an 'echoConsumer' is revoked for a specific 'tokenId'.\n     */\n    \nevent\n PermissionRevoked(address \nindexed\n operator, address \nindexed\n echoConsumer, uint256 \nindexed\n tokenId);\n// 方法：拓展场景使用echo的接口\n    \n/**\n     * @d","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-lucus"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774789793888}}
{"type":"message","id":"1c9fea10","parentId":"726499bf","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:10:16.064Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The document is quite long and contains a lot of content about ECHO contract interfaces. Let me summarize the key points and create a new Feishu doc with the summary. Let me first get the full content more cleanly.\n\nLet me organize what I've read so far:\n\n1. ECHO接口 (ECHO Interface)\n   - 1.1 资产创建和租用 (Asset Creation and Rental) - mint, createDerivative, rentEcho, authorizedAsUser, selfDerive\n   - 1.2 费用、状态设置更新 (Fee and Status Settings) - updateRentalInfo, setExtensible, setDerivTerms, setProtectedSourceURI, setBlueprintURI\n   - 1.3 使用权管理 (Usage Rights Management) - IECHO interface with userOf, useECHO, getRentableStatus, getRentalInfo, etc.\n   - 1.4 可租赁+分润模块 (Rentable + Revenue Split) - IECHORentable interface\n   - 1.5 拓展权授权 (Extension Authorization) - IECHOPermissioned interface\n\nI can see the document continues with more sections, but it's cut off. Let me try extracting the rest of the content to get the complete picture.","thinkingSignature":"c9aac23a7dc7b5a769cb64e9c6824cabe35d5a016e433eec85b8d1c4d84c3076"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_axuc29o5zf0a_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport zipfile\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\n\npath = '/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/ECHOå_çº_æ_å---b2466f79-4d40-43e5-9081-651cbfbc8dea.docx'\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(path, 'r') as z:\n    with z.open('word/document.xml') as f:\n        content = f.read().decode('utf-8')\n        print(f\"Total XML length: {len(content)}\")\n        \n        # Try to extract text with paragraph structure\n        tree = ET.fromstring(content)\n        ns = 'http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main'\n        \n        paragraphs = []\n        for para in tree.iter(f'{{{ns}}}p'):\n            para_text = ''\n            for t in para.iter(f'{{{ns}}}t'):\n                if t.text:\n                    para_text += t.text\n            if para_text.strip():\n                paragraphs.append(para_text)\n        \n        full_text = '\\n'.join(paragraphs)\n        print(f\"Extracted text length: {len(full_text)}\")\n        print(full_text[20000:])\nEOF","timeout":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":59377,"output":545,"cacheRead":11562,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":71484,"cost":{"input":0.0178131,"output":0.000654,"cacheRead":0.00069372,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.019160819999999995}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774789793893,"responseId":"061857a2f1ddaa681c2a533542795de2"}}
{"type":"message","id":"9a744081","parentId":"1c9fea10","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:10:16.183Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_axuc29o5zf0a_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Total XML length: 438013\nExtracted text length: 46260\nto use the ECHO 'tokenId'.     *     * @param echoConsumer The consumption scenario contract for ECHO token.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token.     *      * Emits a {PermissionApproval} event.     */    function approvePermission(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId) external;// 方法：撤销某个场景的授权    /**     * @dev Revokes the permission of a business scenarios to use the 'tokenId'.     *      * Emits a {PermissionRevoked} event.     */    function revokePermission(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId) external;// 方法：查询一个拓展场景是否已被授权    /**     * @dev Returns whether a given consumer contract is authorized to use a specific ECHO token.     *      * @param echoConsumer The address of the consumer contract.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token.     * @return True if the consumer contract is authorized to use the token, false otherwise.     */    function isPermissioned(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId) external view returns (bool);// 方法：查询已授权的拓展场景    /**     * @dev Returns the approved consumers list of the token 'tokenId'.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     */    function getApprovedConsumers(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (address[] memory);}\n1.6 拓展权申请\n申请\n由子合约调用父合约的 requestAsDerivative\n流程：\n_requireOwned(tokenId) 确保父 token 存在\n_requireDerivAllowed(tokenId) 确认允许衍生\n生成 DerivativeRequest，状态标记为 Pending\n存储到 _derivativeRequest[tokenId][index_]\n把 index 推进 _pendingRequest[tokenId] 队列\nemit DerivativeRequested(...)\n批准 / 拒绝\n由父 token 的 owner 调用：\napproveDerivativeRequest\nrejectDerivativeRequest\n流程（批准）：\n_requireOwner(msg.sender, _tokenId) 校验权限\n检查request状态是否 Pending\n更新状态为 Approved\n从 _pendingRequest 移除\n添加 child 到父的 _derivativeGraph\n通知 child 合约 buildParentGraph\nemit DerivativeApproved(...)\n流程（拒绝）：\n_requireOwner(msg.sender, _tokenId) 校验权限\n检查请求状态是否 Pending\n更新状态为 Rejected\n从 _pendingRequest 移除\nemit DerivativeRejected(...)\nSolidity// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT// DimAI ECHO Contracts (last updated v1.0.0) (/ECHO/extensions/interfaces/IECHOPermissionRequestable.sol)pragma solidity ^0.8.20;import {IECHOPermissioned} from \"./IECHOPermissioned.sol\"; interface IECHOPermissionRequestable is IECHOPermissioned { // 类型：拓展许可请求结构       struct PermissionRequest {        address requester;    // Who submitted the request         RequestStatus status; // Status of the request        uint256 requestAt;    // Timestamp of the request        uint256 sceneShare;   // The scene share ratio submitted by a requester , 1000 basis points = 10%        address sceneBeneficiary; // The beneficiary address for the scene, whose share of the rental fee will be distributed.      }// 类型：请求状态枚举    /**     * @dev Enum representing the status of a permission request.     *      *  - None: No request has been made.     *  - Pending: A request has been submitted and is awaiting approval.     *  - Approved: The request has been approved by the token owner.     *  - Rejected: The request has been explicitly rejected.     *  - Cancelled: The request has been cancelled by the requester.     */    enum RequestStatus { None, Pending, Approved, Rejected, Cancelled }// 自定义错误：    /// @dev Error thrown when a permission request already exists for the given tokenId and echoConsumer.    error RequestExists(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer);        /// @dev Error thrown when the number of pending requests exceeds the allowed limit.    error PendingRequestExceed(uint256 tokenId, uint256 pendingCount, uint256 maxPending);    /// @dev Error thrown when handle a permission request which is not pending status.    error RequestNotPending(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer);    /// @dev Error thrown when handle a permission request which is not approved status.    error RequestNotApproved(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer, RequestStatus status);    /**     * @dev Scene beneficiary address for a token is not supported for update,     *      when the caller is not the sence requester, or the RequestStatus is not Approved.     */    error UnsupportedStatus(address caller, address requester, RequestStatus status);    /// @dev Error thrown when the scene share exceeds the maximum allowed value.    error SceneShareExceed(uint256 sceneShare);// 事件：发起请求触发    /**     * @dev Emitted when a permission request is made by a requester for a specific tokenId.     *      * @param requester The address of the entity making the request.     * @param consumer  The contract of the consumer requesting permission.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being requested.     */    event PermissionRequested(address indexed requester, address indexed consumer, uint256 tokenId);    // 事件：拒绝请求触发    /**     * @dev Emitted when a permission request is rejected by the token owner.     *      * @param operator The address of the entity rejecting the request.     * @param consumer The contract of the consumer whose request is being rejected.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being requested.     */    event PermissionRejected(address indexed operator, address indexed consumer, uint256 indexed tokenId);// 事件：场景受益人信息更新时触发    /**     * @dev Emitted when the beneficiary address for the scene of the 'tokenId' is updated.     * @notice This function can only be called by the requester of the permission。     *      * @param operator The address of the operator updating the beneficiary.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token.     * @param echoConsumer The address of the consumer contract.     * @param newBeneficiary The address to set as the new beneficiary.     * @param oldBeneficiary The address of the old beneficiary.     */     event SceneBeneficiaryUpdated(        address operator,        uint256 indexed tokenId,        address indexed echoConsumer,        address newBeneficiary,        address oldBeneficiary    );// 方法：向tokenId发起拓展请求    /**     * @notice  Allows a echoConsumer to request permission to use an ECHO token.     * @dev This function is designed for permissioned business scenarios,      *      where the echoConsumer can request permission to use the ECHO token 'tokenId'.     *      * @param echoConsumer The contract of the consumer requesting permission.          * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being requested.     * @param proposedShare The proposed share ratio intended for usage in the scenario, 1000 basis points = 10%.     *       Before confirmation, it won't affect actual distribution logic.     *      * Requirements:     * - The proposedShare must be less than 5000 (50%).     *      */    function requestPermission(address echoConsumer, uint256 proposedShare, uint256 tokenId) external;    // 方法：获取tokenId上的待确认场景    /**     * @dev Returns the pending consumers list of the token 'tokenId'.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     */       function getPendingConsumers(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (address[] memory);// 方法：授权echoConsumer在tokenId的拓展请求    /**     * @notice  Approves a permission request for a specific ECHO token.     * @dev This function is designed for permissioned business scenarios,      * where the token owner can approve a echoConsumer's request to use the ECHO token 'tokenId'.     *          * @param echoConsumer The contract of the echoConsumer requesting permission.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     */    function approvePermissionRequest(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId) external;  // 方法：拒绝echoConsumer在tokenId的拓展请求     /**     * @notice  Rejects a permission request for a specific ECHO token.     * @dev This function is designed for permissioned business scenarios,      * where the token owner can reject a echoConsumer's request to use the ECHO token 'tokenId'.     *          * @param echoConsumer The contract of the echoConsumer requesting permission.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     *      * Emits a {PermissionRejected} event.     */    function rejectPermissionRequest(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId) external;  // 方法：撤销echoConsumer在tokenId的拓展请求     /**     * @dev Revokes the permission of a business scenarios to use the 'tokenId'.     *      * Emits a {PermissionRevoked} event.     */    function revokePermissionRequest(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId) external;// 方法：获取待确认的拓展场景    /**     * @dev Returns the pending consumers list of the token 'tokenId'.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     */       function getPendingConsumers(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (address[] memory);    // 方法：获取echoConsumer在tokenId的拓展请求详情    /**     * @dev Returns the permission request details for a specific echoConsumer and tokenId.     *      * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     * @param echoConsumer The contract of the echoConsumer requesting permission.     */    function getPermissionRequest(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer) external view returns (PermissionRequest memory);// 方法：更新拓展场景受益人信息    /**     * @dev Update the beneficiary address for the scene of the 'tokenId'.     * @notice This function can only be called by the requester of the permission。     *      * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token.     * @param echoConsumer The address of the consumer contract.     * @param beneficiary The address to set as the beneficiary.     */     function updateSceneBeneficiary(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer, address beneficiary) external;// 方法：查询场景受益人信息，分润比例，受益人地址    /**     * @dev Gets the beneficiary address for the consumer scene of the tokenId.     * @notice Only returns a valid result when `_permissionRequest`'s status is `RequestStatus.Approved`.     *      * @return sceneShare The share ratio for the scene.     * @return sceneBeneficiary The address of the beneficiary.     */     function getBeneficiaryInfo(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer) external view returns (uint256 sceneShare, address sceneBeneficiary);    }\n1.7 拓展使用和分润\nJava// 方法：拓展场景使用echo的接口    /**     * @dev Use the 'tokenId' ECHO in an echoConsumer contract.     *      * @param user The address of the user who is using the ECHO token.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     *      */    function useECHOOf(address user, uint256 tokenId) external returns (string memory);// 事件：拓展场景分润事件/** * @dev Emitted when usage revenue is distributed to the scene beneficiary. * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token for which the usage revenue was distributed. * @param paymentToken The address of the payment token used for the rental. * @param sceneShare The amount of usage revenue distributed to the scene beneficiary. * @param scenceContract The contract address of the usage scenarios. */event RevenueDistributedForScene(    uint256 indexed tokenId,     address indexed paymentToken,     uint256 sceneShare,     address scenceContract);\n1.8 衍生权管理\nSolidity// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT// DimAI ECHO Contracts (last updated v1.0.0) (/ECHO/extensions/interfaces/IECHODerivable.sol)pragma solidity ^0.8.20;import {IECHO} from \"../../IECHO.sol\";interface IECHODerivable is IECHO {// 衍生请求的状态枚举类型    enum ReqStatus {         None,             Pending,          Approved,         Rejected     }// 定位资产的结构体    struct EchoAsset {        uint256 tokenId;        address assetContract;    }// 衍生图谱结构体    struct DerivativeGraph {        EchoAsset[] parents;        EchoAsset[] children;    }// 衍生请求结构    struct DerivativeRequest {        address requester;        ReqStatus reqStatus;        uint64 requestedAt;        EchoAsset derivative;        bytes requestData;     }// 衍生条款：记录衍生收费信息    struct DerivativeTerms {        uint256 upfrontFee;     // One-time derivation fee, upfront cost (in wei) to create a derivative of this token.        address paymentToken; // The token address to pay the upfront fee.        uint256 usageRoyalty;   // Share of revenue (in basis points, 100 = 1%) from the usage of this token's derivatives.    }// 衍生品属性：是否为衍生品、是否为未授权衍生品、是否允许衍生、被衍生请求的历史次数、衍生条款    struct DerivAttributes {        bool isDerivative;       // Whether the token is a derivative.        bool isUnlicensed;       // Indicates whether the derivative was created without full authorization from its parent assets.        bool isderivAllowed;     // Whether derivation is allowed for the token.        uint64 requestCount;     // The count of derivative requests made to this token.        DerivativeTerms terms;   // The derivation terms (upfront fee, usage royalty).    }// 自定义错误：    /// @dev Error thrown when the caller is not a contract.    error NotContractCaller();    /// @dev Error thrown when the 'tokenId' is not fully authorized by its parent assets.    error UnlicensedDerivative(uint256 tokenId);    /**     * @notice Error thrown when a target contract does not support derivation.     * @param targetContract The address of the contract that lacks derivation support.     */    error DerivationNotSupport(address targetContract);    /**     * @notice Error thrown when a token ID is not allowed to derive.     * @param tokenId The token ID that attempted the derivation.     */    error DerivationNotAllowed(uint256 tokenId);        /**     * @notice Error thrown when a parent asset is not already declared by tokenId.     */    error ParentNotDeclared(uint256 tokenId, EchoAsset parent);    /**     * @notice Error thrown when a caller is not the parent contract of the token.     * @param caller The address of the caller that attempted to call the function.     * @param neeeded The address of the parent contract that was expected.     */    error CallerNotParentContract(address caller, address neeeded);    /**     * @notice Error thrown when an operation expects a pending derivative request but the request is not pending.     * @param tokenId The token ID associated with the request.     * @param requestId The ID of the derivative request.     */    error ReqNotPending(uint256 tokenId, uint256 requestId);    /**     * @notice Error thrown when the number of pending requests exceeds the allowed limit.     * @param tokenId The token ID associated with the requests.     * @param pendingCount The current number of pending requests.     * @param maxPending The maximum allowed number of pending requests.     */    error PendingRequestLimited(uint256 tokenId, uint256 pendingCount, uint256 maxPending);    /**     * @notice Error indicating a token is attempting to derive from itself, which is not allowed.     * @param tokenId The ID of the token that references itself in its parent list.     * @param assetContract The contract address of the token that references itself.     */    error DerivativeSelfReference(uint256 tokenId, address assetContract);    /**     * @notice Error thrown when the total royalty of the parents exceeds 100% (10000 bps).     */    error TotalRoyaltyExceed(uint256 totalRoyalty);// 事件：衍生白名单添加事件     /**     * @notice Emitted when an account is authorized or deauthorized as a deriver for a specific token.     * @param tokenId The token ID for which to set deriver authorization.     * @param account The address of the account being authorized or deauthorized.     * @param authorized A boolean indicating whether the account was authorized (true) or deauthorized (false).     */    event DeriverAuthorized(uint256 indexed tokenId, address account, bool authorized);   // 事件：衍生品创建时触发    /**     * @notice Emitted when a new derivative asset is created.     * @param owner The address of the owner who created the derivative.     * @param tokenId The unique identifier of the newly created derivative asset.     * @param declaredParents An array of EchoAssets that were declared as parents for this derivative.     */    event DerivativeCreated(address indexed owner, uint256 tokenId, EchoAsset[] declaredParents);    // 事件：衍生条款更新时触发，包括开/关衍生权限    /**     * @notice Emitted when updating the derivative terms and enabling/disabling derivation for a specific token.     *      * @param tokenId The unique identifier id of the token .     * @param enabled Boolean indicating whether derivation is enabled (true) or disabled (false).     * @param terms The DerivativeTerms struct containing upfront fee, payment token, and usage royalty.     */    event DerivTermsUpdated(uint256 indexed tokenId, bool enabled, DerivativeTerms terms);// 发起衍生请求时触发    /**     * @notice Emitted when a new derivatiove request is submitted for a given parent token.     * @param tokenId The token ID of the parent asset receiving the request.     * @param requestIndex The index of the derivative request.     * @param derivativeRequest The full request details including requester, child, and metadata.     */    event DerivativeRequested(uint256 indexed tokenId, uint256 requestIndex, DerivativeRequest derivativeRequest);// 事件：衍生请求被批准时触发    /**       * @notice Emitted when a derivative request is approved by the parent token’s owner.     * @param operator The address that approved the request (parent token owner).     * @param parent The parent asset being derived from.     * @param requester The original requester who submitted the derivative request.     * @param child The child asset that has been approved as a derivative.     */    event DerivativeApproved(address indexed operator, EchoAsset parent, address requester, EchoAsset child);    // 事件：衍生请求拒绝时触发    /**      * @notice Emitted when a derivative request is rejected by the parent token’s owner.     * @param operator The address that rejected the request (parent token owner).     * @param parent The parent asset being derived from.     * @param requester The original requester who submitted the derivative request.     * @param child The child asset whose request was rejected.     */    event DerivativeRejected(address indexed operator, EchoAsset parent, address requester, EchoAsset child);// 方法：更新一个衍生者的授权状态    /**      * @notice Authorizes or revokes an account as a special deriver a specific token.     * @dev Only the owner or an approved operator of the token can call this function.     *      * @param tokenId The token ID for which the authorization is set.     * @param account The address of the account to authorize or revoke.     * @param authorized Boolean indicating whether to authorize (true) or revoke (false) the account.     *      *  Emits a {DeriverAuthorized} event.     */    function setDeriverAuth(uint256 tokenId, address account, bool authorized) external;// 方法：检查一个账户是否为衍生白名单用户    /**      * @dev Checks whether 'account' is authorized as a special deriver for 'tokenId'.     */    function isAuthorizedDeriver(uint256 tokenId, address account) external view returns (bool);// 方法： 更新衍生条款       /**     * @notice Sets the derivative terms and enables/disables derivation for a specific token.     * @notice Only update terms if derivation is enabled.     * @notice If disabling, pass in empty ‘terms’ (all zeroes).     * @dev Only the owner or an approved operator of the token can call this function.     *      * @param tokenId The token ID for which to set derivative terms.     * @param enabled Boolean indicating whether to enable (true) or disable (false) derivation.     * @param terms The DerivativeTerms struct containing upfront fee, payment token, and usage royalty.                *      * Emits either a {DerivationEnabled} or {DerivationDisabled} event based on the 'enabled' parameter.     */    function setDerivTerms(uint256 tokenId, bool enabled, DerivativeTerms calldata terms) external;   // 方法：获取衍生品一些状态属性    /**      * @notice Returns the derivative attributes for a specific token.     * @dev Returns whether the token is a derivative, whether derivation is allowed,     *      the count of derivative requests, and the derivative terms.     *      * @param tokenId The token ID to retrieve attributes for.     *      * @return DerivAttributes, includes:     * - isDerivative Whether the token is a derivative.     * - isUnlicensed Indicates whether the derivative was created without full authorization      *      from its parent assets. When `true`, this token is considered an unlicensed derivative (e.g., pirated),     *      and may be restricted from usage or further derivation.     * - isderivAllowed Whether derivation is allowed for the token.     * - requestCount The count of derivative requests made to this token.     * - terms The derivative terms (upfront fee, usage royalty).     */    function getDerivAttrs(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (DerivAttributes memory);  //  方法：建立衍生图谱（ 此方法外部限制使用，仅已声明的父代资产合约可调用）    /**     * @notice Establishes a child->parent link for a given token.     * @dev Can only be called by the parent asset’s contract. Verifies that the parent has been previously declared,     *      removes it from the declared list, and formally adds it to the token’s parent graph.     *      * @param tokenId The token ID of the child asset (derivative).     * @param parent The parent EchoAsset to link to the child.     */    function buildParentGraph(uint256 tokenId, EchoAsset memory parent) external; // 方法：获取tokenId的待确认亲代     /**     * @dev Get the parents of a 'tokenId' that declared but not yet confirmed.     */     function getDeclaredParents(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (EchoAsset[] memory);// 方法： 获取衍生图谱    /**     * @dev Returns the full derivative graph (parents and children) for the specified tokenId.      * @param tokenId The ID of the token for which to retrieve the derivative graph.     */    function getDerivativeGraph(uint256 tokenId) external view returns(EchoAsset[] memory parents, EchoAsset[] memory children);//  方法： 获取亲代分润表     /**      * @dev Get the parent share list of a 'tokenId'.     * @notice The parent share list contains each parent's tokenId, contract address, and usage royalty (bps).     * @notice The total usage royalty of all parents must not exceed 10000 bps (100%).     *      * @param tokenId The ID of the token for which to retrieve parent shares.     * @return An array of AssetShare structs representing the parent shares.     */    function getParentShareList(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (AssetShare[] memory);// 方法：获取（亲代）tokenId上待处理的衍生请求      /**     * @dev Get the pending requests list of a 'tokenId'.     *      * @param tokenId The ID of the token for which to retrieve pending requests.     * @return An array of pending request ID.     */    function getPendingRequests(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (uint256[] memory); // 方法：查看衍生请求    /**     * @dev Get a tokenId's derivative request on request ID 'requestId'.     *     This function retrieves the details of a specific derivative request for a given token ID.     *      * @param tokenId The ID of the token for which to retrieve the derivative request.     * @param requestId The id of the derivative request in the pending requests list.     */    function getDerivativeRequest(uint256 tokenId, uint256 requestId) external view returns (DerivativeRequest memory);    // 方法：亲求衍生，此方法外部使用受限    /**     * @notice Only contract(child ECHO) can call this function to request derivative from a specific parent token.     * @dev Direct calls from EOAs are not allowed; only contracts are permitted.     *      * @dev Registers a derivative request targeting the given parent ‘tokenId’, indicating that the provided child EchoAsset      *      ‘_derivative’ wants to become a derivative of it. The request is stored and marked as pending in the parent contract.     * @param tokenId The parent token to which the derivative is being requested.     * @param _derivative The child EchoAsset that wants to derive from the parent.     * @param _reqData  Encoded request data for the derivative request, containing:      *      1. requester address (the origin of the request)     *      2. child token URI (string)     *      * Emit a {DerivativeRequested} event.     */    function requestAsDerivative(uint256 tokenId, EchoAsset memory _derivative, bytes memory _reqData) external;    // 方法：批准衍生请求      /**     * @notice Approves a pending derivative request for a given parent token.     * @dev Can only be called by the owner of the parent token. Marks the request as approved,     *      removes it from the pending list, adds the child asset to the parent’s derivative graph,     *      and notifies the child contract to establish the parent graph.     *      * @param _tokenId The token ID of the parent asset.     * @param requestId The ID of the derivative request to approve.     *      * Emit a {DerivativeApproved} event.     */    function approveDerivativeRequest(uint256 _tokenId, uint256 requestId) external;    // 方法：拒绝衍生    /**     * @notice Rejects a pending derivative request for a given parent token.     * @dev Can only be called by the owner of the parent token. Marks the request as rejected     *      and removes it from the pending queue. No further action is taken on the child asset.     *      * @param _tokenId The token ID of the parent asset.     * @param requestId The ID of the derivative request to reject.     *      * Emit a {DerivativeRejected} event.     */    function rejectDerivativeRequest(uint256 _tokenId, uint256 requestId) external;}\n1.9 衍生分润\nJava// 事件：衍生费支付事件/** * @dev Emitted when a derivation fee is paid to the receiver. *  * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token that incurred the derivation fee. * @param payer The address of the payer who paid the derivation fee. * @param receiver The address of the receiver who received the derivation fee. * @param amount The amount of the derivation fee that was paid. * @param paymentToken The address of the token used for the payment. */event DerivFeePaid(    uint256 tokenId,    address indexed payer,    address indexed receiver,    uint256 amount,    address paymentToken);// 事件：亲代分润事件/** * @notice Derivation scenarios exists. * @dev Emitted when usage revenue is distributed to the parents. * @param childTokenId The ID of the derivative token for which rental income is being distributed. * @param paymentToken The address of the token used for payment. * @param parent The parent ECHO asset that received a share of the revenue. * @param parentShare The amount of rental fee distributed to the parent ECHO token owner. */event DerivRevenueDistributed(    uint256 indexed childTokenId,     address indexed paymentToken,      EchoAsset parent,    uint256 parentShare);"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":112,"aggregated":"Total XML length: 438013\nExtracted text length: 46260\nto use the ECHO 'tokenId'.     *     * @param echoConsumer The consumption scenario contract for ECHO token.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token.     *      * Emits a {PermissionApproval} event.     */    function approvePermission(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId) external;// 方法：撤销某个场景的授权    /**     * @dev Revokes the permission of a business scenarios to use the 'tokenId'.     *      * Emits a {PermissionRevoked} event.     */    function revokePermission(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId) external;// 方法：查询一个拓展场景是否已被授权    /**     * @dev Returns whether a given consumer contract is authorized to use a specific ECHO token.     *      * @param echoConsumer The address of the consumer contract.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token.     * @return True if the consumer contract is authorized to use the token, false otherwise.     */    function isPermissioned(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId) external view returns (bool);// 方法：查询已授权的拓展场景    /**     * @dev Returns the approved consumers list of the token 'tokenId'.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     */    function getApprovedConsumers(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (address[] memory);}\n1.6 拓展权申请\n申请\n由子合约调用父合约的 requestAsDerivative\n流程：\n_requireOwned(tokenId) 确保父 token 存在\n_requireDerivAllowed(tokenId) 确认允许衍生\n生成 DerivativeRequest，状态标记为 Pending\n存储到 _derivativeRequest[tokenId][index_]\n把 index 推进 _pendingRequest[tokenId] 队列\nemit DerivativeRequested(...)\n批准 / 拒绝\n由父 token 的 owner 调用：\napproveDerivativeRequest\nrejectDerivativeRequest\n流程（批准）：\n_requireOwner(msg.sender, _tokenId) 校验权限\n检查request状态是否 Pending\n更新状态为 Approved\n从 _pendingRequest 移除\n添加 child 到父的 _derivativeGraph\n通知 child 合约 buildParentGraph\nemit DerivativeApproved(...)\n流程（拒绝）：\n_requireOwner(msg.sender, _tokenId) 校验权限\n检查请求状态是否 Pending\n更新状态为 Rejected\n从 _pendingRequest 移除\nemit DerivativeRejected(...)\nSolidity// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT// DimAI ECHO Contracts (last updated v1.0.0) (/ECHO/extensions/interfaces/IECHOPermissionRequestable.sol)pragma solidity ^0.8.20;import {IECHOPermissioned} from \"./IECHOPermissioned.sol\"; interface IECHOPermissionRequestable is IECHOPermissioned { // 类型：拓展许可请求结构       struct PermissionRequest {        address requester;    // Who submitted the request         RequestStatus status; // Status of the request        uint256 requestAt;    // Timestamp of the request        uint256 sceneShare;   // The scene share ratio submitted by a requester , 1000 basis points = 10%        address sceneBeneficiary; // The beneficiary address for the scene, whose share of the rental fee will be distributed.      }// 类型：请求状态枚举    /**     * @dev Enum representing the status of a permission request.     *      *  - None: No request has been made.     *  - Pending: A request has been submitted and is awaiting approval.     *  - Approved: The request has been approved by the token owner.     *  - Rejected: The request has been explicitly rejected.     *  - Cancelled: The request has been cancelled by the requester.     */    enum RequestStatus { None, Pending, Approved, Rejected, Cancelled }// 自定义错误：    /// @dev Error thrown when a permission request already exists for the given tokenId and echoConsumer.    error RequestExists(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer);        /// @dev Error thrown when the number of pending requests exceeds the allowed limit.    error PendingRequestExceed(uint256 tokenId, uint256 pendingCount, uint256 maxPending);    /// @dev Error thrown when handle a permission request which is not pending status.    error RequestNotPending(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer);    /// @dev Error thrown when handle a permission request which is not approved status.    error RequestNotApproved(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer, RequestStatus status);    /**     * @dev Scene beneficiary address for a token is not supported for update,     *      when the caller is not the sence requester, or the RequestStatus is not Approved.     */    error UnsupportedStatus(address caller, address requester, RequestStatus status);    /// @dev Error thrown when the scene share exceeds the maximum allowed value.    error SceneShareExceed(uint256 sceneShare);// 事件：发起请求触发    /**     * @dev Emitted when a permission request is made by a requester for a specific tokenId.     *      * @param requester The address of the entity making the request.     * @param consumer  The contract of the consumer requesting permission.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being requested.     */    event PermissionRequested(address indexed requester, address indexed consumer, uint256 tokenId);    // 事件：拒绝请求触发    /**     * @dev Emitted when a permission request is rejected by the token owner.     *      * @param operator The address of the entity rejecting the request.     * @param consumer The contract of the consumer whose request is being rejected.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being requested.     */    event PermissionRejected(address indexed operator, address indexed consumer, uint256 indexed tokenId);// 事件：场景受益人信息更新时触发    /**     * @dev Emitted when the beneficiary address for the scene of the 'tokenId' is updated.     * @notice This function can only be called by the requester of the permission。     *      * @param operator The address of the operator updating the beneficiary.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token.     * @param echoConsumer The address of the consumer contract.     * @param newBeneficiary The address to set as the new beneficiary.     * @param oldBeneficiary The address of the old beneficiary.     */     event SceneBeneficiaryUpdated(        address operator,        uint256 indexed tokenId,        address indexed echoConsumer,        address newBeneficiary,        address oldBeneficiary    );// 方法：向tokenId发起拓展请求    /**     * @notice  Allows a echoConsumer to request permission to use an ECHO token.     * @dev This function is designed for permissioned business scenarios,      *      where the echoConsumer can request permission to use the ECHO token 'tokenId'.     *      * @param echoConsumer The contract of the consumer requesting permission.          * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being requested.     * @param proposedShare The proposed share ratio intended for usage in the scenario, 1000 basis points = 10%.     *       Before confirmation, it won't affect actual distribution logic.     *      * Requirements:     * - The proposedShare must be less than 5000 (50%).     *      */    function requestPermission(address echoConsumer, uint256 proposedShare, uint256 tokenId) external;    // 方法：获取tokenId上的待确认场景    /**     * @dev Returns the pending consumers list of the token 'tokenId'.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     */       function getPendingConsumers(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (address[] memory);// 方法：授权echoConsumer在tokenId的拓展请求    /**     * @notice  Approves a permission request for a specific ECHO token.     * @dev This function is designed for permissioned business scenarios,      * where the token owner can approve a echoConsumer's request to use the ECHO token 'tokenId'.     *          * @param echoConsumer The contract of the echoConsumer requesting permission.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     */    function approvePermissionRequest(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId) external;  // 方法：拒绝echoConsumer在tokenId的拓展请求     /**     * @notice  Rejects a permission request for a specific ECHO token.     * @dev This function is designed for permissioned business scenarios,      * where the token owner can reject a echoConsumer's request to use the ECHO token 'tokenId'.     *          * @param echoConsumer The contract of the echoConsumer requesting permission.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     *      * Emits a {PermissionRejected} event.     */    function rejectPermissionRequest(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId) external;  // 方法：撤销echoConsumer在tokenId的拓展请求     /**     * @dev Revokes the permission of a business scenarios to use the 'tokenId'.     *      * Emits a {PermissionRevoked} event.     */    function revokePermissionRequest(address echoConsumer, uint256 tokenId) external;// 方法：获取待确认的拓展场景    /**     * @dev Returns the pending consumers list of the token 'tokenId'.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     */       function getPendingConsumers(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (address[] memory);    // 方法：获取echoConsumer在tokenId的拓展请求详情    /**     * @dev Returns the permission request details for a specific echoConsumer and tokenId.     *      * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     * @param echoConsumer The contract of the echoConsumer requesting permission.     */    function getPermissionRequest(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer) external view returns (PermissionRequest memory);// 方法：更新拓展场景受益人信息    /**     * @dev Update the beneficiary address for the scene of the 'tokenId'.     * @notice This function can only be called by the requester of the permission。     *      * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token.     * @param echoConsumer The address of the consumer contract.     * @param beneficiary The address to set as the beneficiary.     */     function updateSceneBeneficiary(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer, address beneficiary) external;// 方法：查询场景受益人信息，分润比例，受益人地址    /**     * @dev Gets the beneficiary address for the consumer scene of the tokenId.     * @notice Only returns a valid result when `_permissionRequest`'s status is `RequestStatus.Approved`.     *      * @return sceneShare The share ratio for the scene.     * @return sceneBeneficiary The address of the beneficiary.     */     function getBeneficiaryInfo(uint256 tokenId, address echoConsumer) external view returns (uint256 sceneShare, address sceneBeneficiary);    }\n1.7 拓展使用和分润\nJava// 方法：拓展场景使用echo的接口    /**     * @dev Use the 'tokenId' ECHO in an echoConsumer contract.     *      * @param user The address of the user who is using the ECHO token.     * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token being used.     *      */    function useECHOOf(address user, uint256 tokenId) external returns (string memory);// 事件：拓展场景分润事件/** * @dev Emitted when usage revenue is distributed to the scene beneficiary. * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token for which the usage revenue was distributed. * @param paymentToken The address of the payment token used for the rental. * @param sceneShare The amount of usage revenue distributed to the scene beneficiary. * @param scenceContract The contract address of the usage scenarios. */event RevenueDistributedForScene(    uint256 indexed tokenId,     address indexed paymentToken,     uint256 sceneShare,     address scenceContract);\n1.8 衍生权管理\nSolidity// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT// DimAI ECHO Contracts (last updated v1.0.0) (/ECHO/extensions/interfaces/IECHODerivable.sol)pragma solidity ^0.8.20;import {IECHO} from \"../../IECHO.sol\";interface IECHODerivable is IECHO {// 衍生请求的状态枚举类型    enum ReqStatus {         None,             Pending,          Approved,         Rejected     }// 定位资产的结构体    struct EchoAsset {        uint256 tokenId;        address assetContract;    }// 衍生图谱结构体    struct DerivativeGraph {        EchoAsset[] parents;        EchoAsset[] children;    }// 衍生请求结构    struct DerivativeRequest {        address requester;        ReqStatus reqStatus;        uint64 requestedAt;        EchoAsset derivative;        bytes requestData;     }// 衍生条款：记录衍生收费信息    struct DerivativeTerms {        uint256 upfrontFee;     // One-time derivation fee, upfront cost (in wei) to create a derivative of this token.        address paymentToken; // The token address to pay the upfront fee.        uint256 usageRoyalty;   // Share of revenue (in basis points, 100 = 1%) from the usage of this token's derivatives.    }// 衍生品属性：是否为衍生品、是否为未授权衍生品、是否允许衍生、被衍生请求的历史次数、衍生条款    struct DerivAttributes {        bool isDerivative;       // Whether the token is a derivative.        bool isUnlicensed;       // Indicates whether the derivative was created without full authorization from its parent assets.        bool isderivAllowed;     // Whether derivation is allowed for the token.        uint64 requestCount;     // The count of derivative requests made to this token.        DerivativeTerms terms;   // The derivation terms (upfront fee, usage royalty).    }// 自定义错误：    /// @dev Error thrown when the caller is not a contract.    error NotContractCaller();    /// @dev Error thrown when the 'tokenId' is not fully authorized by its parent assets.    error UnlicensedDerivative(uint256 tokenId);    /**     * @notice Error thrown when a target contract does not support derivation.     * @param targetContract The address of the contract that lacks derivation support.     */    error DerivationNotSupport(address targetContract);    /**     * @notice Error thrown when a token ID is not allowed to derive.     * @param tokenId The token ID that attempted the derivation.     */    error DerivationNotAllowed(uint256 tokenId);        /**     * @notice Error thrown when a parent asset is not already declared by tokenId.     */    error ParentNotDeclared(uint256 tokenId, EchoAsset parent);    /**     * @notice Error thrown when a caller is not the parent contract of the token.     * @param caller The address of the caller that attempted to call the function.     * @param neeeded The address of the parent contract that was expected.     */    error CallerNotParentContract(address caller, address neeeded);    /**     * @notice Error thrown when an operation expects a pending derivative request but the request is not pending.     * @param tokenId The token ID associated with the request.     * @param requestId The ID of the derivative request.     */    error ReqNotPending(uint256 tokenId, uint256 requestId);    /**     * @notice Error thrown when the number of pending requests exceeds the allowed limit.     * @param tokenId The token ID associated with the requests.     * @param pendingCount The current number of pending requests.     * @param maxPending The maximum allowed number of pending requests.     */    error PendingRequestLimited(uint256 tokenId, uint256 pendingCount, uint256 maxPending);    /**     * @notice Error indicating a token is attempting to derive from itself, which is not allowed.     * @param tokenId The ID of the token that references itself in its parent list.     * @param assetContract The contract address of the token that references itself.     */    error DerivativeSelfReference(uint256 tokenId, address assetContract);    /**     * @notice Error thrown when the total royalty of the parents exceeds 100% (10000 bps).     */    error TotalRoyaltyExceed(uint256 totalRoyalty);// 事件：衍生白名单添加事件     /**     * @notice Emitted when an account is authorized or deauthorized as a deriver for a specific token.     * @param tokenId The token ID for which to set deriver authorization.     * @param account The address of the account being authorized or deauthorized.     * @param authorized A boolean indicating whether the account was authorized (true) or deauthorized (false).     */    event DeriverAuthorized(uint256 indexed tokenId, address account, bool authorized);   // 事件：衍生品创建时触发    /**     * @notice Emitted when a new derivative asset is created.     * @param owner The address of the owner who created the derivative.     * @param tokenId The unique identifier of the newly created derivative asset.     * @param declaredParents An array of EchoAssets that were declared as parents for this derivative.     */    event DerivativeCreated(address indexed owner, uint256 tokenId, EchoAsset[] declaredParents);    // 事件：衍生条款更新时触发，包括开/关衍生权限    /**     * @notice Emitted when updating the derivative terms and enabling/disabling derivation for a specific token.     *      * @param tokenId The unique identifier id of the token .     * @param enabled Boolean indicating whether derivation is enabled (true) or disabled (false).     * @param terms The DerivativeTerms struct containing upfront fee, payment token, and usage royalty.     */    event DerivTermsUpdated(uint256 indexed tokenId, bool enabled, DerivativeTerms terms);// 发起衍生请求时触发    /**     * @notice Emitted when a new derivatiove request is submitted for a given parent token.     * @param tokenId The token ID of the parent asset receiving the request.     * @param requestIndex The index of the derivative request.     * @param derivativeRequest The full request details including requester, child, and metadata.     */    event DerivativeRequested(uint256 indexed tokenId, uint256 requestIndex, DerivativeRequest derivativeRequest);// 事件：衍生请求被批准时触发    /**       * @notice Emitted when a derivative request is approved by the parent token’s owner.     * @param operator The address that approved the request (parent token owner).     * @param parent The parent asset being derived from.     * @param requester The original requester who submitted the derivative request.     * @param child The child asset that has been approved as a derivative.     */    event DerivativeApproved(address indexed operator, EchoAsset parent, address requester, EchoAsset child);    // 事件：衍生请求拒绝时触发    /**      * @notice Emitted when a derivative request is rejected by the parent token’s owner.     * @param operator The address that rejected the request (parent token owner).     * @param parent The parent asset being derived from.     * @param requester The original requester who submitted the derivative request.     * @param child The child asset whose request was rejected.     */    event DerivativeRejected(address indexed operator, EchoAsset parent, address requester, EchoAsset child);// 方法：更新一个衍生者的授权状态    /**      * @notice Authorizes or revokes an account as a special deriver a specific token.     * @dev Only the owner or an approved operator of the token can call this function.     *      * @param tokenId The token ID for which the authorization is set.     * @param account The address of the account to authorize or revoke.     * @param authorized Boolean indicating whether to authorize (true) or revoke (false) the account.     *      *  Emits a {DeriverAuthorized} event.     */    function setDeriverAuth(uint256 tokenId, address account, bool authorized) external;// 方法：检查一个账户是否为衍生白名单用户    /**      * @dev Checks whether 'account' is authorized as a special deriver for 'tokenId'.     */    function isAuthorizedDeriver(uint256 tokenId, address account) external view returns (bool);// 方法： 更新衍生条款       /**     * @notice Sets the derivative terms and enables/disables derivation for a specific token.     * @notice Only update terms if derivation is enabled.     * @notice If disabling, pass in empty ‘terms’ (all zeroes).     * @dev Only the owner or an approved operator of the token can call this function.     *      * @param tokenId The token ID for which to set derivative terms.     * @param enabled Boolean indicating whether to enable (true) or disable (false) derivation.     * @param terms The DerivativeTerms struct containing upfront fee, payment token, and usage royalty.                *      * Emits either a {DerivationEnabled} or {DerivationDisabled} event based on the 'enabled' parameter.     */    function setDerivTerms(uint256 tokenId, bool enabled, DerivativeTerms calldata terms) external;   // 方法：获取衍生品一些状态属性    /**      * @notice Returns the derivative attributes for a specific token.     * @dev Returns whether the token is a derivative, whether derivation is allowed,     *      the count of derivative requests, and the derivative terms.     *      * @param tokenId The token ID to retrieve attributes for.     *      * @return DerivAttributes, includes:     * - isDerivative Whether the token is a derivative.     * - isUnlicensed Indicates whether the derivative was created without full authorization      *      from its parent assets. When `true`, this token is considered an unlicensed derivative (e.g., pirated),     *      and may be restricted from usage or further derivation.     * - isderivAllowed Whether derivation is allowed for the token.     * - requestCount The count of derivative requests made to this token.     * - terms The derivative terms (upfront fee, usage royalty).     */    function getDerivAttrs(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (DerivAttributes memory);  //  方法：建立衍生图谱（ 此方法外部限制使用，仅已声明的父代资产合约可调用）    /**     * @notice Establishes a child->parent link for a given token.     * @dev Can only be called by the parent asset’s contract. Verifies that the parent has been previously declared,     *      removes it from the declared list, and formally adds it to the token’s parent graph.     *      * @param tokenId The token ID of the child asset (derivative).     * @param parent The parent EchoAsset to link to the child.     */    function buildParentGraph(uint256 tokenId, EchoAsset memory parent) external; // 方法：获取tokenId的待确认亲代     /**     * @dev Get the parents of a 'tokenId' that declared but not yet confirmed.     */     function getDeclaredParents(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (EchoAsset[] memory);// 方法： 获取衍生图谱    /**     * @dev Returns the full derivative graph (parents and children) for the specified tokenId.      * @param tokenId The ID of the token for which to retrieve the derivative graph.     */    function getDerivativeGraph(uint256 tokenId) external view returns(EchoAsset[] memory parents, EchoAsset[] memory children);//  方法： 获取亲代分润表     /**      * @dev Get the parent share list of a 'tokenId'.     * @notice The parent share list contains each parent's tokenId, contract address, and usage royalty (bps).     * @notice The total usage royalty of all parents must not exceed 10000 bps (100%).     *      * @param tokenId The ID of the token for which to retrieve parent shares.     * @return An array of AssetShare structs representing the parent shares.     */    function getParentShareList(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (AssetShare[] memory);// 方法：获取（亲代）tokenId上待处理的衍生请求      /**     * @dev Get the pending requests list of a 'tokenId'.     *      * @param tokenId The ID of the token for which to retrieve pending requests.     * @return An array of pending request ID.     */    function getPendingRequests(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (uint256[] memory); // 方法：查看衍生请求    /**     * @dev Get a tokenId's derivative request on request ID 'requestId'.     *     This function retrieves the details of a specific derivative request for a given token ID.     *      * @param tokenId The ID of the token for which to retrieve the derivative request.     * @param requestId The id of the derivative request in the pending requests list.     */    function getDerivativeRequest(uint256 tokenId, uint256 requestId) external view returns (DerivativeRequest memory);    // 方法：亲求衍生，此方法外部使用受限    /**     * @notice Only contract(child ECHO) can call this function to request derivative from a specific parent token.     * @dev Direct calls from EOAs are not allowed; only contracts are permitted.     *      * @dev Registers a derivative request targeting the given parent ‘tokenId’, indicating that the provided child EchoAsset      *      ‘_derivative’ wants to become a derivative of it. The request is stored and marked as pending in the parent contract.     * @param tokenId The parent token to which the derivative is being requested.     * @param _derivative The child EchoAsset that wants to derive from the parent.     * @param _reqData  Encoded request data for the derivative request, containing:      *      1. requester address (the origin of the request)     *      2. child token URI (string)     *      * Emit a {DerivativeRequested} event.     */    function requestAsDerivative(uint256 tokenId, EchoAsset memory _derivative, bytes memory _reqData) external;    // 方法：批准衍生请求      /**     * @notice Approves a pending derivative request for a given parent token.     * @dev Can only be called by the owner of the parent token. Marks the request as approved,     *      removes it from the pending list, adds the child asset to the parent’s derivative graph,     *      and notifies the child contract to establish the parent graph.     *      * @param _tokenId The token ID of the parent asset.     * @param requestId The ID of the derivative request to approve.     *      * Emit a {DerivativeApproved} event.     */    function approveDerivativeRequest(uint256 _tokenId, uint256 requestId) external;    // 方法：拒绝衍生    /**     * @notice Rejects a pending derivative request for a given parent token.     * @dev Can only be called by the owner of the parent token. Marks the request as rejected     *      and removes it from the pending queue. No further action is taken on the child asset.     *      * @param _tokenId The token ID of the parent asset.     * @param requestId The ID of the derivative request to reject.     *      * Emit a {DerivativeRejected} event.     */    function rejectDerivativeRequest(uint256 _tokenId, uint256 requestId) external;}\n1.9 衍生分润\nJava// 事件：衍生费支付事件/** * @dev Emitted when a derivation fee is paid to the receiver. *  * @param tokenId The ID of the ECHO token that incurred the derivation fee. * @param payer The address of the payer who paid the derivation fee. * @param receiver The address of the receiver who received the derivation fee. * @param amount The amount of the derivation fee that was paid. * @param paymentToken The address of the token used for the payment. */event DerivFeePaid(    uint256 tokenId,    address indexed payer,    address indexed receiver,    uint256 amount,    address paymentToken);// 事件：亲代分润事件/** * @notice Derivation scenarios exists. * @dev Emitted when usage revenue is distributed to the parents. * @param childTokenId The ID of the derivative token for which rental income is being distributed. * @param paymentToken The address of the token used for payment. * @param parent The parent ECHO asset that received a share of the revenue. * @param parentShare The amount of rental fee distributed to the parent ECHO token owner. */event DerivRevenueDistributed(    uint256 indexed childTokenId,     address indexed paymentToken,      EchoAsset parent,    uint256 parentShare);","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-lucus"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774789816180}}
{"type":"message","id":"cdda7eb8","parentId":"9a744081","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:10:29.454Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the ECHO contract interfaces. Let me create a summary document in Feishu. The document covers:\n\n1. ECHO Interface Overview\n2. Asset Creation and Rental (1.1)\n3. Fee and Status Settings (1.2)\n4. Usage Rights Management (1.3)\n5. Rentable + Revenue Split Module (1.4)\n6. Extension Authorization (1.5)\n7. Extension Permission Requests (1.6)\n8. Extension Usage and Revenue Distribution (1.7)\n9. Derivative Rights Management (1.8)\n10. Derivative Revenue Distribution (1.9)\n\n\nI'll write this summary directly to the existing Hello World document since the user asked me to read and summarize the content into a document.","thinkingSignature":"9b4cfe8466a36b59c673c69ba99b0343963d2ddec8baf031fb19b93c70fd58dc"},{"type":"text","text":"文档读取完成，内容很丰富。现在直接在 Hello World 文档里写入总结：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_k7lmmrkr0p98_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s --max-time 15 \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/KFZ5dQFLtoCey1xV5Nfjl0nTp8f/blocks?document_revision_id=-1&page_size=50\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer t-g2073td3EKILAO7NBFLGV5SNRALOBZCKUNI6VDP4\" 2>&1 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(json.dumps([b['block_id'] for b in d['data']['items']], indent=2))\"","timeout":20}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":66048,"output":348,"cacheRead":11562,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":77958,"cost":{"input":0.0198144,"output":0.00041759999999999996,"cacheRead":0.00069372,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02092572}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774789816185,"responseId":"061857b873ef0cfbc8367e1b33ba22a2"}}
