{"type":"message","id":"0e38ea67","parentId":"6c4d10b0","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:48:16.894Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me try the correct API endpoint. Based on Feishu docs, to move a file, the API is:\n`POST /open-apis/drive/v1/files/{file_token}/move`\n\nWith body:\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"docx\",\n  \"parent_token\": \"{target_folder_token}\"\n}\n```\n\nFor the personal root (\"我的文档库\"), the parent_token is typically empty string, but that gave us a param error. \n\nActually, looking at this more carefully - maybe the issue is that the document is owned by the bot, and the user doesn't have permission to move it. Even though we gave the user `full_access` permission on the document, that might not include the ability to move it to a different folder if the user doesn't have write access to that destination folder.\n \nI should check what folders the user actually has access to, or try using a valid folder token from their existing folder structure. Since we can see the current parent is `nodjpaHe7MntogaRuHkK6FaF8cd`, maybe I can pass that same token to keep the document in its current location instead of moving it.","thinkingSignature":"4afc2ff5bcb51b47d6a5ddc3c71eb07b5c375cd5e4d08644221ab2edbe2a76f8"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_i90naqagxv4v_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s --max-time 15 \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/files/C3FQdU5TEogY5LxpZCHj6x3BpVc/move\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer t-g2073td3EKILAO7NBFLGV5SNRALOBZCKUNI6VDP4\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -X POST \\\n  -d '{\"type\":\"docx\",\"parent_token\":\"nodjpaHe7MntogaRuHkK6FaF8cd\"}' 2>&1","timeout":20}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":102869,"output":401,"cacheRead":11562,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":114832,"cost":{"input":0.030860699999999998,"output":0.0004812,"cacheRead":0.00069372,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.03203562}},"stopR