{"type":"message","id":"66f4124e","parentId":"483c8ae8","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:53:22.243Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is saying I should find their user token myself. But wait - there's no way for me to \"find\" a user's token. The token is a secret that only the user has access to. I can't just query it from the API without user credentials.\n\nLet me think about this. When we authenticated earlier, we used the tenant access token (app-level token), not a user token. User tokens require OAuth flow where the user logs in and grants permission.\n\nActually, maybe the user is joking? Or maybe they're suggesting I should have asked earlier and stored it? But that's not really how it works.\n\nActually, I think the user might be saying \"you're the AI agent, figure it out yourself\" - but in this case it's technically impossible. User tokens are obtained through OAuth 2.0 flow and are specific to each user's login session.\n\n\nI need to be direct with them - user tokens aren't something I can retrieve on my own, they require an explicit OAuth authorization flow where the user enters their credentials. That's the only way to get one.","thinkingSignature":"a25e78f09ee1671a096e14aaf36f458b5045d6e48ace6a8814bb2eef9339b548"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 这个我真没法自己查——用户 token 需要你亲自授权才能拿到，API 没办法主动获取。\n\n**最快的方式**：你在飞书文档里手动操作一下，右上角「···」→「移动」，选「我的文档库」，10秒搞定。\n\n或者如果你想给我长期权限，可以走一次 OAuth 授权。以后操作飞书文档就不用每次问你确认了。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":43,"output":297,"cacheRead":11562,"cacheWrite":102858,"totalTokens":114760,"cost":{"input":0.0000129,"output":0.0003564,"cacheRead":0.00069372,"cacheWrite":0.03857175,"total":0.03963477}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774792384653,"responseId":"061861c1edc90dcfc18fbe4e2f32e014"}}
