9130105098ae6fa4d566956\",\"parent_token\":\"nodjpaHe7MntogaRuHkK6FaF8cd\",\"token\":\"C3FQdU5TEogY5LxpZCHj6x3BpVc\",\"type\":\"docx\",\"url\":\"https://ijpsec7x2d72.jp.larksuite.com/docx/C3FQdU5TEogY5LxpZCHj6x3BpVc\"},{\"created_time\":\"1774789626\",\"modified_time\":\"1774790117\",\"name\":\"Hello World\",\"owner_id\":\"ou_07c0309729130105098ae6fa4d566956\",\"parent_token\":\"nodjpaHe7MntogaRuHkK6FaF8cd\",\"token\":\"KFZ5dQFLtoCey1xV5Nfjl0nTp8f\",\"type\":\"docx\",\"url\":\"https://ijpsec7x2d72.jp.larksuite.com/docx/KFZ5dQFLtoCey1xV5Nfjl0nTp8f\"}],\"has_more\":false},\"msg\":\"success\"}","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-lucus"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774792656839}}
{"type":"message","id":"a472e0dc","parentId":"88e8638e","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:57:51.086Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The new document `CUXnd71hloNZTzxMdtZjB2sFpxb` is still in the same folder `nodjpaHe7MntogaRuHkK6FaF8cd`. It seems the `owner_open_id` doesn't affect where the document is created. The document is still in the bot's folder.\n\nLet me check if this folder is the user's personal space or the bot's space. Actually, all these docs are in the same folder `nodjpaHe7MntogaRuHkK6FaF8cd`. The user can access them because they have `full_access` permission on the individual documents, but they can't move them because they don't have write access to the folder itself.\n \nI'm realizing the core issue: the bot's API always creates documents in its own folder, and while I can grant users permissions to individual documents, folder-level permissions require a different approach—either the user takes action themselves or I need to find a way to create documents directly in their space instead of the bot's. a folder token.\n\nActually, the most straightforward solution: **delete the old document and rename the new one**... no that won't help since it's the same folder.\n\nLet me just grant the user full_access to the new document (already done since it was created with owner_open_id) and tell the user that both documents are in the same folder. If they can access the folder, they can move it. If not, they can at least access and edit the new document.\n\nActually, let me just focus on what I can do: the new document `CUXnd71hloNZTzxMdtZjB2sFpxb` was created. The user should be able to access it since it was created with their `owner_open_id`. Let me verify they have access to the new document.","thinkingSignature":"a3d7a3a85d7b1679921779b4d846dfa5c9f975f641235626077b46ca641e5d1f"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_yurkgz41de4n_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s --max-time 15 \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/permissions/CUXnd71hloNZTzxMdtZjB2sFpxb/members?type=docx\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer t-g2073td3EKILAO7NBFLGV5SNRALOBZCKUNI6VDP4\" 2>&1","timeout":20}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":105235,"output":502,"cacheRead":11562,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":117299,"cost":{"input":0.0315705,"output":0.0006024,"cacheRead":0.00069372,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.032866620000000006}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774792656849,"responseId":"061862d18f04508ef86acf6b6c0997e2"}}
