{"type":"message","id":"18655903","parentId":"4b4e1c5d","timestamp":"2026-03-29T14:16:43.344Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to know where to get their OAuth token. For Feishu, getting a user OAuth token typically requires going through the OAuth authorization flow. Let me think about the best way to guide them.\n\nFor Feishu OAuth, the typical flow involves:\n1. The app redirects the user to an authorization URL\n2. The user grants permission\n3. The app receives an authorization code\n4. The app exchanges the code for a user access token\n\nHowever, since this is a bot/app context, the user might not have a web app set up to receive the redirect. For personal use, they could:\n\n1. Use the Feishu developer console to get their own user token (but this is typically for developers)\n\n\n2. Alternatively, they could just move the documents manually through the Feishu app interface, which would be simpler than setting up OAuth. But if they want a more sustainable solution, I'd need to explain the OAuth flow and how to set up the app credentials properly, or check if there's a simpler way to get a user token through the existing bot setup.\n\nFor Feishu, getting a user token usually requires going through an OAuth authorization flow where the user logs in and grants permission, but since this is running as a bot, that redirect-based flow won't work without a web server. Let me just explain the manual approach first since it's more practical here, and keep the OAuth explanation as an alternative if they really need programmatic access to their personal space. The core issue is that the bot's API can't create documents in the user's personal space without their OAuth token, and setting that up requires a web server to handle the callback. I should give them a practical answer about the simplest way to move forward.","thinkingSignature":"0d6d0edca7b26c8353672d5bc6e66f169d3d6bfd0fcb793184aa2a12a62b2005"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 说实话，Feishu 的 OAuth 需要你有一个能接收回调的服务器，对个人用户来说比较麻烦。\n\n**最简单的方式**：\n\n你在飞书 app 里，手动把文档移动到你的个人文档库。步骤：\n1. 打开文档 → 右上角「···」→「移动」\n2. 选择「我的文档库」或任意你想放的文件夹\n3. 确认\n\n这个操作只需要你点几下，10秒完成，不需要任何 token。\n\n---\n\n如果你之后真的需要我长期有权限操作你的飞书个人空间，可以走一次 OAuth 授权流程——需要你有个服务器或者用 ngrok 做本地回调。那个时候我们再折腾这个。\n\n现在先把文档手动移一下？"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":43,"output":502,"cacheRead":3800,"cacheWrite":113321,"totalTokens":117666,"cost":{"input":0.0000129,"output":0.0006024,"cacheRead":0.00022799999999999999,"cacheWrite":0.042495375,"total":0.043338675}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774793777226,"responseId":"06186732b236a8fd5e2167bc501ae81d"}}
