{"type":"message","id":"5e3cf34f","parentId":"071c81d2","timestamp":"2026-03-29T14:21:31.775Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is suggesting whether I can put documents in an organization's public/shared area instead. The Feishu app has a \"shared space\" (云文档空间) concept. Let me try to create the document in the shared/organizational space instead of the bot's folder.\n\nLooking at the Feishu API, when creating a document, you can specify `folder_token` to put it in a specific folder. If I can find a shared/organizational folder token, I could use that.\n\nActually, looking at the file listing earlier, the documents were all in a folder with `parent_token: \"nodjpaHe7MntogaRuHkK6FaF8cd\"`. \n\nBut maybe I can skip specifying a folder entirely and create it in the root of the shared space, or I could try getting a list of all folders and see if there's a shared space I can access.","thinkingSignature":"a10cd4c21a5347b68414df86c33c94c43793a51455bd101d2db18bf3a6cf171e"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_uy5ya1ujr56m_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s --max-time 15 \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/drive/v1/files?page_size=20&fetch_children=true\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer t-g2073td3EKILAO7NBFLGV5SNRALOBZCKUNI6VDP4\" 2>&1","timeout":20}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":43,"output":286,"cacheRead":117627,"cacheWrite":265,"totalTokens":118221,"cost":{"input":0.0000129,"output":0.0003432,"cacheRead":0.00705762,"cacheWrite":0.000099375,"total":0.007513094999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774794077459,"responseId":"0618685ec6a1e426a3c9a1064df93e6b"}}
